 `compose-pr-body`.\",\ndocs/specs/workspace.json:106:      \"criterion\": \"A Cargo package belongs to the workspace its `package.workspace` names, else to the nearest `Cargo.toml` at or above its directory, never above the workspace root, that has a `workspace` table (the package itself counts); it need not be the root's. A `version.workspace = true` or `{ workspace = true }` dependency resolves against that workspace's `[workspace.package]` and `[workspace.dependencies]`, and a version or dependency spec rewrite is written to that workspace's manifest. A package that inherits when no such workspace exists, whose `package.workspace` names no workspace or leaves the root, or whose ancestors cannot be read or parsed, fails with E313 naming the package.\",\ndocs/specs/versioning.json:221:      \"criterion\": \"Before the first write, every file the plan edits, creates or deletes is checked: a manifest must exist as a readable regular file, no path may be a symbolic link or sit beneath one (Git cannot stage it), no path may leave the workspace, the directory of each written file (or its nearest existing parent) must take a new file, and a file the plan stages must not be ignored by a .gitignore unless Git already tracks it. Checking creates no file or directory. Any failure stops the run with E314 naming every such path, and nothing has been written, staged or deleted. A lockfile that a .gitignore ignores is still refreshed on disk but is not staged. The checks cover only what can be known beforehand: a lockfile refresh that fails (E208) or a Git command that fails while staging can still stop the run after the writes.\",\ndocs/specs/versioning.json:236:      \"criterion\": \"Planning fails with E315 in a shallow clone when any package infers its bump from commits (`release-trigger = \\\"auto\\\"`), because the commit window would be shorter than the real one. Packages that take their bump from changesets alone are unaffected.\",\ndocs/projects/V1-SYSTEM-HARDENING.json:45:        \"Implement ADR 12's canonical-reference contract with one owner-aware resolver: canonical required in config, groups, rules, product and artifact packages, report and matrix keys and CLI arguments; colon rejected with a code that names the slash form (E316); a bare reference in config rejected with a fix-it (E317). Changesets and pre.json keep native names resolved at read time, with a hard error for colon. Platform-manifest npm names in groups stay native. Do not change tag names.\",\ndocs/errors.md:306:| E310 | Failed to read manifest `<path>`: <message> | Make the manifest readable UTF-8 text; a workspace member's manifest is never skipped. |\ndocs/errors.md:307:| E311 | Invalid workspace membership in `<path>`: <message> | Make `members`/`exclude` (Cargo, uv) or `workspaces`/`packages` (npm, pnpm) an array of valid glob strings; Callisto will not guess which packages a malformed workspace admits. |\ndocs/errors.md:308:| E312 | Package `<path>` is reached through a symbolic link, which Git cannot stage | Replace the link with the real directory, or list it in a .gitignore under the workspace root so discovery skips it; Callisto cannot commit a version bump to a file beneath a symbolic link. |\n---\ndocs/errors.md  41.6K\n304:| E308 | `release build-python` or `artifact-manifest --seal-python` on an intent that publishes no Python package | drop --seal-python and `release build-python` for an intent without a Python publish |\n305:| E309 | `release build-python` run with `--dry-run`, which cannot write build output | re-run `callisto release build-python` without --dry-run |\n306:| E310 | Failed to read manifest `<path>`: <message> | Make the manifest readable UTF-8 text; a workspace member's manifest is never skipped. |\n307:| E311 | Invalid workspace membership in `<path>`: <message> | Make `members`/`exclude` (Cargo, uv) or `workspaces`/`packages` (npm, pnpm) an array of valid glob strings; Callisto will not guess which packages a malformed workspace admits. |\n308:| E312 | Package `<path>` is reached through a symbolic link, which Git cannot stage | Replace the link with the real directory, or list it in a .gitignore under the workspace root so discovery skips it; Callisto cannot commit a version bump to a file beneath a symbolic link. |\n309:| E313 | The workspace is incomplete: N manifest(s) could not be resolved | Fix or remove the manifests named above and re-run; Callisto will not plan a release from a partial workspace. |\n310:| E314 | Cannot apply the version plan: N file(s) cannot be written, so nothing was changed | Fix the files named above (a missing file, permissions, a symbolic link Git cannot stage, or a path a .gitignore ignores) and re-run; no manifest, changelog or changeset was touched. |\n311:| E315 | Commit-based version inference needs the full Git history, but this repository is a shallow clone | Fetch the full history (`git fetch --unshallow`, or `fetch-depth: 0` for actions/checkout), or give the packages that need no commit inference `release-trigger = \"changeset\"`. |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"classifierBoundary":true,"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"02a0e0fd-78b6-4301-af61-e71fc695a4a2","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-colon","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-colon","branch":"fix/reject-colon-references","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"example/x","visibility":"unknown"},{"host":"github.com","rem