ckage` (#13).**\n  - `crates/callisto-cli/tests/release_command_e2e_tests.rs:449,451`, `a_dry_run_after_a_failed_tag_push_plans_the_remaining_operations` (`release --package cargo:core-crate`)\n  - `crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/release.rs:713`, `parse_release_selection_accepts_colon_as_an_alias_of_slash` (unit test; its doc comment is at 707)\n  - The assertions in release.rs:719, `parse_release_selection_rejects_a_bare_name`, are the bare-name case, not colon.\n  \n  **`[[fixed-group]]` and `[[linked-group]]` members (#9).**\n  - `crates/callisto-graph/tests/config_resolve_tests.rs:128`, `conflicting_fixed_group_membership_across_spellings_is_rejected`\n  - `crates/callisto-graph/tests/config_resolve_tests.rs:167`, `conflicting_membership_across_fixed_and_linked_groups_is_rejected`\n  - `crates/callisto-graph/src/walk/tests.rs:32`, `fixed_group_member_resolves_via_prefixed_unpromoted_cargo_package` (`cargo:foo`)\n  - `crates/callisto-graph/src/walk/tests.rs:71`, `fixed_group_member_naming_absent_ecosystem_is_missing_group_member`. It uses `npm:foo` and asserts at line 82 that the error echoes `member == \"npm:foo\"`.\n  \n  **`[[package]] match` (#11).**\n  - `crates/callisto-graph/src/walk/tests.rs:953`, `package_rule_matching_no_ecosystem_the_package_has_gets_a_matched_nothing_diagnostic` (`pypi:foo`)\n  - `crates/callisto-graph/src/walk/tests.rs:1318`, `prefixed_package_rules_still_apply_correctly_to_promoted_siblings` (`cargo:native-core`, `npm:native-core`)\n  - `crates/callisto-graph/src/config/resolve.rs:1177`, `resolve_package_config_prefixed_rule_does_not_apply_to_a_different_ecosystem_package` (`pypi:foo`)\n  - `crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate/tests.rs:1473`, `test_pre_major_inference_prefixed_beats_bare_when_bare_declared_first` (`npm:pkg`)\n  \n  **`[[package-set]] match` (#12).**\n  - `crates/callisto-graph/tests/package_set_ecosystem_test.rs:59`, `ecosystem_prefixed_package_set_matching_nothing_emits_diagnostic` (`npm:internal-*`). It also asserts that the message contains the colon pattern at line 84.\n  - `crates/callisto-graph/tests/package_set_ecosystem_test.rs:113`, `ecosystem_prefixed_package_set_matching_real_package_applies_and_is_silent` (`cargo:internal-*`)\n  - `crates/callisto-graph/src/config/pattern.rs:100`, `ecosystem_prefixed_pattern_matches_only_that_ecosystem`\n  - `crates/callisto-graph/src/config/pattern.rs:120`, `slash_separated_pattern_matches_the_same_as_colon_separated`. I did not open this body; the name and its location suggest it feeds a colon pattern.\n  \n  **Resolver unit tests (#2).**\n  - `crates/callisto-graph/src/identity.rs:98`, `resolve_qualified_selector_is_exact_and_misses_report_e102` (`index.resolve(\"npm:foo\")`, \"eco:name must be accepted as an alias\")\n  - `identity.rs:20` and `identity.rs:32`: the `resolve_human_*` tests, which are dead-code coverage.\n  - `crates/callisto-graph/src/walk/tests.rs:800`, `unpromoted_standalone_cargo_package_retains_bare_id` (`resolve_human(\"cargo:single\")`)\n  \n  **`add --package` (#7), `matrix --package` (#8), `product-package` and `[[release.artifact]] package` (#10).** No test passes a colon string through any of these three.\n  \n  **Not selector input (false positives).**\n  - `crates/callisto-cli/tests/native_resolution_e2e_tests.rs:662-672,882-883` use `npm:@protocol/lib@^x`, which is an npm alias dependency spec.\n  - Model tests that call `PackageId::parse(\"cargo:x\")` for fixtures:\n    - `crates/callisto-graph/tests/apply_persist_open_count_test.rs`\n    - `crates/callisto-graph/src/apply/**/tests.rs`\n    - `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release_decision.rs:1247,1626,1631,1665`\n    - `crates/callisto-model/src/identity.rs:440-474`, `package_id_schema_describes_bare_and_qualified_strings`\n    - `crates/callisto-model/src/release/package_id.rs:275` (asserts rejection)\n  \n  ## 3. Docs, spec and dogfood files showing the colon form\n  \n  **No colon form (grep-verified):** root `callisto.toml` (all slash: `product-package = \"cargo/callisto-cli\"`, three `[[release.artifact]]` entries, `[[package]] match = \"cargo/callisto-cli\"`; the fixed group uses bare names), `AGENTS.md`, `README.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `docs/config.md`, `docs/releasing.md`, `docs/errors.md`, `.github/**`, `.changeset/*.md`, `crates/callisto-cli/tests/cmd/help.trycmd` (the only trycmd), and all `*.snap` files (init workflow, release derive, pr_body).\n  \n  **Colon form appears:**\n  - `docs/specs/workspace.json:23`, \"`<ecosystem>/<name>` and `<ecosystem>:<name>` select the package whether or not it is promoted\"\n  - `docs/specs/workspace.json:30`, `match = \"<name>\" | \"<ecosystem>:<name>\" | \"<ecosystem>/<name>\"`\n  - `docs/specs/workspace.json:38-39`, package-set glob, colon and slash both scope\n  - `docs/specs/workspace.json:128`, the group member criterion \"`cargo:foo` or `cargo/foo` resolves…\"\n  - `docs/specs/workspace.json:138`, the diagnostic lists candidates \"(`cargo:foo`)\". This is an output claim, see section 4.\n  - `docs/specs/cli.json:72`, `callisto release [--package <ECOSYSTEM/NAME>|<ECOSYSTEM:NAME>]...`\n  - `docs/architecture/identity.md:16` (table example `cargo:foo`), `identity.md:30` (`cargo:foo` and `npm:foo` as separate packages), `identity.md:18` (parse prefix text)\n  - `crates/callisto-graph/CHANGELOG.md:287,351`. These are historical entries; the first says \"qualify it with `npm:name`\".\n  - Source comments or messages:\n    - `crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/release.rs:199` (error detail text)\n    - `crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/release.rs:707`\n    - `crates/callisto-graph/src/config/pattern.rs:10,17,25,52,53`\n    - `crates/callisto-graph/src/config/resolve.rs:306`\n  \n  **Docs that already say colon is rejected, the target state:**\n  - `docs/adr/0012-canonical-distribution-release-ownership.md:13` (\"Reject the colon form everywhere\")\n  - `docs/architecture/polyglot-v1.md:18`\n  - `docs/projects/V1-IMPLEMENTATION.md:23`\n  - `docs/projects/V1-SYSTEM-HARDENING.json:45` (new code E316 \"colon rejected with a code that names the slash form\", E317 for a bare config reference; \"Changesets and pre.json keep native names resolved at read time, with a hard error for colon\")\n  - `docs/projects/ROAD-TO-V1.md:48`\n  \n  E316 and E317 are not yet in `docs/errors.md`. Per those docs, a hard colon error is required for changesets and `pre.json` as well, even though bare native names stay allowed there.\n  \n  ## 4. Output that renders a colon-form id\n  \n  Everything that renders a `PackageId` goes through `display_name()` and so gives the slash form:\n  - JSON via `Serialize` (identity.rs:232)\n  - `Display`\n  - tags (`tag.rs:74`)\n  - matrix keys (`graph/src/matrix.rs:498,504,536`; `model/src/matrix.rs:12` doc)\n  - CLI tables (`cli/src/render/mod.rs:42,77,96,113`)\n  - errors (`graph/src/error.rs:77,91,98,117,128,135,151,168`)\n  - the PR body\n  - `pre_json_key` (`lib.rs:293`)\n  - the changeset entry written by `add` (`add.rs:40`)\n  - `ReleasePackageId` `Display` (`release/package_id.rs:84`, slash)\n  \n  **One colon emitter:** `crates/callisto-graph/src/identity.rs:483-487`, in `IdentityIndex::resolve_native_with_fallback`. It does `format!(\"{}:{n}\", e.prefix())` and builds the `UnknownPackage` warning \"dependency name `x` is ambiguous across ecosystems: cargo:foo, pypi:foo\". It appears in the `status`, `version` and `matrix` diagnostics lists. The name is a dependency name from a manifest, not a user selector, and a nearby comment explicitly says no prefix advice is given. A user might still copy `cargo:foo` back as a selector. It is pinned by these assertions:\n  - `identity.rs:76-77`, `resolve_native_with_fallback_returns_none_and_one_diagnostic_for_two_candidates`\n  - `identity.rs:187,192`, `resolve_native_with_fallback_lists_the_candidates_own_native_name_not_the_primary_name`\n  - `walk/tests.rs:1216,1245`, `npm_consumer_depending_on_cargo_only_name_gets_no_edge_and_diagnostic` and `npm_consumer_depending_on_serde_with_cargo_serde_present_gets_no_edge_and_diagnostic`\n  - `crates/callisto-graph/tests/ecosystem_bugs_test.rs:308`, `cross_ecosystem_npm_to_cargo_dep_edge_is_discovered` (`cargo:rust-addon`)\n  - `docs/specs/workspace.json:138`\n  \n  **Echoes of user input:** a group member written with colon is echoed as typed in `MissingGroupMember` (`walk/tests.rs:82` asserts `\"npm:foo\"`). The `package-set` \"matched nothing\" diagnostic (`walk.rs` near 789-798 and the `package_set_ecosystem_test.rs:84,130` assertions) echoes the user's raw colon pattern. Its advice text already says \"use an ecosystem-prefixed pattern like `{eco}/{name}`\" (slash).\n  \n  I did not find a status, version `--dry-run`, matrix or release-plan JSON field that prints a colon-form package id.\n</agent-message>"}
