q_011CgEm5UuQvos5uUWgALSvu","type":"assistant","uuid":"9e097584-3e7a-4752-9a5a-f96d7d326565","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:35:40.983Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-colon","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.292","gitBranch":"fix/reject-colon-references","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"9e097584-3e7a-4752-9a5a-f96d7d326565","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"26ff9d9b-c388-4173-9aa2-ff76b9634f6a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KQZia6SELaBMhA2nXiYeD1","type":"tool_result","content":"--23\n      \"description\": \"Display and selector form: the bare manifest name, or `<ecosystem>/<name>` once another ecosystem declares the same name. JSON output, messages, changeset entries and `pre.json` keys use it; `<ecosystem>/<name>` and `<ecosystem>:<name>` select the package whether or not it is promoted.\",\n--30\n      \"signature\": \"match = \\\"<name>\\\" | \\\"<ecosystem>:<name>\\\" | \\\"<ecosystem>/<name>\\\"\",\n--38\n      \"signature\": \"match = \\\"<glob>\\\" | \\\"<ecosystem>:<glob>\\\" | \\\"<ecosystem>/<glob>\\\"\",\n--39\n      \"description\": \"Glob over package names. The colon and slash forms both scope the glob to an ecosystem; a bare glob matches any ecosystem.\",\n--128\n      \"criterion\": \"A `[[fixed-group]]` or `[[linked-group]]` member written `cargo:foo` or `cargo/foo` resolves to package `foo` when a Cargo manifest declares `foo`, promoted or not, through the same selector resolver used for `--package` and changesets; a member naming an ecosystem with no such manifest fails loading with E108, and a bare member name ambiguous across ecosystems fails loading with E103 (not E108). A group that names one package twice, under the same spelling or under two of its native names, fails loading with E250.\",\n--138\n      \"criterion\": \"A dependency edge is created only to a workspace package that declares the dependency's name in the depending manifest's own ecosystem; a name declared only in other ecosystems creates no edge and one `unknown-package` warning listing the candidates (`cargo:foo`), and an ordinary name no workspace package declares creates no edge and no diagnostic. An explicit pnpm `workspace:` reference that cannot resolve to an admitted npm member creates no edge and emits one `unknown-package` warning.\"\n      \"signature\": \"callisto release [--package <ECOSYSTEM/NAME>|<ECOSYSTEM:NAME>]... [--receipt <FILE>]\",\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `Bare(name)` | `foo`, `@scope/foo` | `None` |\n| `Prefixed { ecosystem, name }` | `cargo:foo`, `npm/@scope/foo` | `Some(e)` |\n\n- `parse` treats text before the first `:` or `/` as a prefix only when `Ecosystem::from_prefix` knows it, so `@scope/foo` stays bare.\n- `display_name` renders a prefixed id as `ecosystem/name`.\n- `PackageId` is the display and selector form; `Package::key()` is the workspace-relative directory of the first canonical manifest. It survives display promotion, not a directory move. `ReleasePackageId` names each canonical distribution as `ecosystem/name` using that manifest's own native name.\n- Default tags use `display_name()`: `foo@{version}` while bare, `cargo/foo@{version}` after promotion. Promotion therefore also changes the namespace of newly created default tags (ADR 11).\n- `matches` is a weak \"could be the same package\" relation, not equality:\n  - Different names never match.\n  - A bare id matches any id with the same name, in either direction: bare is an ecosystem wildcard.\n  - Two prefixed ids match only when their ecosystems are equal.\n- A dual-manifest package can have different native names. `IdentityIndex` resolves each ecosystem/name to its owner; the weak `matches` relation alone does not establish distribution identity or ownership.\n\n## Resolving ambiguity\n\nA workspace can hold `cargo:foo` and `npm:foo` as separate packages; ambiguity is resolved where a lookup happens. Qualified selectors work before and after promotion. Canonical-only new references are planned in [the v1 design](polyglot-v1.md), not implemented by today's parser.\n\n- `aggregate::resolve_target_package` resolves changeset entries through `IdentityIndex::resolve_id`, which maps qualified native distribution names to their owner and rejects ambiguous bare names. `status` attributes changeset entries and checks their well-formedness through the same resolver. `PackageId::resolve_unique` scans display ids, is deprecated, and is not equivalent for dual-manifest packages with different native names.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"31e0edad-a684-467d-9007-eb09ecc2875c","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:35:41.529Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"--23\n      \"description\": \"Display and selector form: the bare manifest name, or `<ecosystem>/<name>` once another ecosystem declares the same name. JSON output, messages, changeset entries and `pre.json` keys use it; `<ecosystem>/<name>` and `<ecosystem>:<name>` select the package whether or not it is promoted.\",\n--30\n      \"signature\": \"match = \\\"<name>\\\" | \\\"<ecosystem>:<name>\\\" | \\\"<ecosystem>/<name>\\\"\",\n--38\n      \"signature\": \"match = \\\"<glob>\\\" | \\\"<ecosystem>:<glob>\\\" | \\\"<ecosystem>/<glob>\\\"\",\n--39\n      \"description\": \"Glob over package names. The colon and slash forms both scope the glob to an ecosystem; a bare glob matches any ecosystem.\",\n--128\n      \"criterion\": \"A `[[fixed-group]]` or `[[linked-group]]` member written `cargo:foo` or `cargo/foo` resolves to package `foo` when a Cargo manifest declares `foo`, promoted or not, through the same selector resolver used for `--package` and changesets; a member naming an ecosystem with no such manifest fails loading with E108, and a bare member name ambiguous across ecosystems fails loading with E103 (not E108). A group that names one package twice, under the same spelling or under two of its native names, fails loading with E250.\",\n--138\n      \"criterion\": \"A dependency edge is created only to a workspace package that declares the dependency's name in the depending manifest's own ecosystem; a name declared only in other ecosystems creates no edge and one `unknown-package` warning listing the candidates (`cargo:foo`), and an ordinary name no workspace package declares creates no edge and no diagnostic. An explicit pnpm `workspace:` reference that cannot resolve to an admitted npm member creates no edge and emits one `unknown-package` warning.\"\n      \"signature\": \"callisto release [--package <ECOSYSTEM/NAME>|<ECOSYSTEM:NAME>]... [--receipt <FILE>]\",\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `Bare(name)` | `foo`, `@scope/foo` | `None` |\n| `Prefixed { ecosystem, name }` | `cargo:foo`, `npm/@scope/foo` | `Some(e)` |\n\n- `parse` treats text before the first `:` or `/` as a prefix only when `Ecosystem::from_prefix` knows it, so `@scope/foo` stays bare.\n- `display_name` renders a prefixed id as `ecosystem/name`.\n- `PackageId` is the display and selector form; `Package::key()` is the workspace-relative directory of the first canonical manifest. It survives display promotion, not a directory move. `ReleasePackageId` names each canonical distribution as `ecosystem/name` using that manifest's own native name.\n- Default tags use `display_name()`: `foo@{version}` while bare, `cargo/foo@{version}` after promotion. Promotion therefore also changes the namespace of newly created default tags (ADR 11).\n- `matches` is a weak \"could be the same package\" relation, not equality:\n  - Different names never match.\n  - A bare id matches any id with the same name, in either direction: bare is an ecosystem wildcard.\n  - Two prefixed ids match only when their ecosystems are equal.\n- A dual-manifest package can have different native names. `IdentityIndex` resolves each ecosystem/name to its owner; the weak `matches` relation alone does not establish distribution identity or ownership.\n\n## Resolving ambiguity\n\nA workspace can hold `cargo:foo` and `npm:foo` as separate packages; ambiguity is resolved where a lookup happens. Qualified selectors work before and after promotion. Canonical-only new references are planned in [the v1 design](polyglot-v1.md), not implemented by today's parser.\n\n- `aggregate::resolve_target_package` resolves changeset entries through `IdentityIndex::resolve_id`, which maps qualified native distribution names to their owner and rejects ambiguous bare names. `status` attributes changeset entries and checks their well-formedness through the same resolver. `PackageId::resolve_unique` scans display ids, is deprecated, and is not equivalent for dual-manifest packages with different native names.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"edd53227-06f5-4fce-9880-cce7dccd0118","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-colon","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-colon","branch":"fix/reject-colon-references","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":17,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"example/x","visibility":"unknown"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"acme/demo-lib","visibility":"unknown"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"acme/vtagdemo","visibility":"unknown"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-colon","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9e097584-3e7a-4752-9a5a-f96d7d326565","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-colon","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.292","gitBranch":"fix/reject-colon-references","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
