{"parentUuid":"c99ae951-b78c-42ed-aae2-e12dd7386278","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFpJo2Y3b6ZLEVcFTjn2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #270 is ready for you to merge. All 12 hosted checks pass, it is not a draft, and GitHub reports it CLEAN. I checked its status just now.\n\n**Done:** all 16 earlier fix PRs are merged, and every commit is signed. #270 is the second of five T06 slices. It rejects the colon form (`cargo:foo`) with E316 and names the slash form.\n\n**Open PRs:**\n- #270: ready to merge.\n- #248: the automated \"version packages\" release PR. I haven't touched it.\n\n**Next:** T06 slice 3 (E317). It would make a bare package name in `callisto.toml` an error, which breaks configs that use bare group members. This repo's own `callisto.toml` is one of them. I haven't started it. Should I go ahead, or leave bare names allowed in config?\n\n**Also pending:**\n- **Plan file:** `.claude/plans/NEXT-WORK.md` still lists the 16 PRs as open. I'll update it after #270 merges.\n- **Decision-free v1 work:** an MSRV CI job, scheduled `cargo deny`, Cargo dependabot, semver-checks in CI, fuzz targets for the manifest editors, and panic hygiene.\n- **Your decisions still open:**\n  - OIDC trusted publishing.\n  - Which crates reach 1.0.\n  - Pre mode on the managed release route.\n  - Snapshot publishing and dist-tag policy.\n  - A schemaVersion bump with T06.\n  - The rest are in section D of `V1-REVIEW-2026-10-20.md`.\n\nresult: PR #270 (colon-reference rejection, E316) has all 12 hosted checks green and is ready to merge; I'm waiting on your call on E317 (bare names in config) before the next T06 slice."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":902,"cache_read_input_tokens":79404,"output_tokens":598,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":