{"parentUuid":"009d4bd4-da58-4547-bd41-b3f6fa676b24","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_015ptietkDNvqP2qYjqrkot3","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"gh pr view 270 --json state,mergedAt,mergeCommit --jq .; rtk git log origin/main --oneline -3; sed -n 1,74p .claude/plans/NEXT-WORK.md\",\"description\":\"Confirm 270 merge state and read plan\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":18},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4e723b99-8a46-4af9-8789-b8439a7ea1ab","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:11:02.970Z","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"stack/docs-v1","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"009d4bd4-da58-4547-bd41-b3f6fa676b24","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"78e7e027-2557-4280-83d1-5eb0c59c8478","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015ptietkDNvqP2qYjqrkot3","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"mergeCommit\":{\"oid\":\"44ab50f93d32cd3655558f14196fe9f09547c263\"},\"mergedAt\":\"2026-10-21T18:11:01Z\",\"state\":\"MERGED\"}\n404aea289 fix(version): report a changeset entry that names no package (#267)\nb813d422a fix(config): reject a group that names one package under two spellings (#266)\na9ba42fb4 fix(manifests): rewrite Poetry carets and keep one-minor Python ranges narrow (#265)\n# Next work after the nested-workspace stack\n\nBaseline: main `308d35a91` (#247). Local only, never PR it. Verified against the code on 2026-10-18; the earlier version of this file (written at 0.10.2) listed work that has since shipped.\n\n## Shipped since the 0.10.2 plan\n\n- W1 apply mixed-routing tests (`apply/tests.rs`, `a_manifest_written_through_both_routes_...`).\n- W2 SYS-RETRY: `incomplete_tagged_releases` observes every operation of packages tagged on HEAD (`release/local.rs`).\n- W3 PYFILES: per-file completeness, partial upload recovery, sealed file sets (#232, #233).\n- W5 R3 and SYS-BARRIER: `derive_release_inputs_with` is a staged pipeline; `OpIndex::tag_prerequisites` makes a dual owner's tag wait for both publishes.\n- W6 R5 and SYS-NAPI: init tests and templates are out of line; the matrix workflow derives napi builds from the intent.\n- W7 R1: `walk.rs::build` is staged (`discover`, `assign_identities`, `resolve_packages`, `build_edges`).\n- Cargo, npm, pnpm and uv workspaces below the repo root, strict reads, ignored-file preflight, shallow-clone guard, unreadable changelog (#241-#247).\n\n## In flight\n\n- #249 PYROUTES: `publish-url` on a `pypi` registry.\n- #250 docs: drop the shipped T09 and T09-ROUTES plan entries.\n\n## Still open and not blocked\n\n- W0 is done once #250 merges. Branch cleanup finished 2026-10-18: 61 merged branches and 11 worktrees removed. Kept on purpose: `docs/crate-consolidation-plan`, `fix/release-consistency`, `refactor/apply-pipeline`, `test/black-box-gaps`, `fix/pypi-per-file-completeness`, `fix/python-declaration-locators` (local commits not in their merged PR heads), `worktree-wave2-base` (3 commits, no upstream), local-only `backup/`, `fix/stack-*`, `pr/*`, `stack/*`, `work/*` branches, `docs/next-work-plan` (locked worktree) and `main` (62 behind).\n- T08 leftover: `link_publish_prerequisites` (`release/derive.rs`) makes a dependent wait on every publish of the dependency package, not only the distribution the edge touches. Over-serializes, never unsafe.\n\n## Blocked on owner decisions\n\n- D01 owner contract: options and leans are in `.claude/plans/D01-DECISIONS.md` (2026-10-20). All of D01 decided 2026-10-20 (A to E, see the Decided table in D01-DECISIONS.md); T06 is unblocked once ADR 12 and the plan record the choices. SYS-OWNER, SYS-DEMOTION and the pre.json alias drop are fixed (#230, #222). D (bare packages adopt bare tags by name, path-exists branch ignores the declared name) is an existing-contract repair under ADR 11, not blocked. ADR 12 stays Proposed until A to C land.\n- W1 real-service credential check: where it runs in CI.\n- W4 redacted provider output: allow-list shape and the persisted wire change.\n- W10: `RewriteKey` discriminator (public API) and Python dev-group tracking.\n- W11 verification (T12, T12-DX): needs credentials and an owner-approved run.\n- Inferred-only or manual version releases in managed CI (policy).\n- Accepted gap: the version-level PyPI read counts a partial file set as present. Callisto tags only after a confirmed complete publish, so only a hand-made tag can expose it.\n- A Cargo workspace nested under a root Cargo workspace is still decided by the root's `members` and `exclude` (agreed with Codex; not changed).\n\n## v1 critical path (2026-10-20; superseded by V1-REVIEW-2026-10-20.md, which adds 13 uncovered defects and 13 owner decisions)\n\nChecked on the real binary at main (0.11.0): exactly the 8 user commands, `publish`/`plan-publish`/`tag`/`filter-plan` gone, `init --yes --versioning ... --workflow` writes a 31-line workflow, `release --dry-run` works on any branch. The plan JSON after #251 is one serial chain: D01 -> T06 -> T06-HISTORY -> T08 -> T12 -> T12-DX.\n\n| Step | What is left | Needs |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| D01 | Decided (A to E). Record in ADR 12, polyglot-v1 and the plan, then T06 is unblocked | A docs PR |\n| Ownership repair (T06-HISTORY residue) | Bare packages adopt bare tags by name; path-exists branch ignores the declared name; pre.json bare key with no historical check | Nothing; existing contract under ADR 11 |\n| T06 | One owner-aware resolver, canonical emission, legacy boundary, 24 spec criteria and about 400 fixtures | B and C |\n| T08 | Package-granular selection, optional plugin barrier edge, `link_publish_prerequisites` over-serialization | E. Changes intent digests, so land before 1.0 |\n| Parallel, small | `GroupTable::from_groups` conflict check, receipt run_attempt wording, moon pin in `.prototools`, rustc target facts, explicit registry kind scope | Nothing except kind scope |\n| Parallel, decisions | W4 redacted provider stderr (persisted wire change), W10 `RewriteKey` and dev-group tracking (public API), managed-CI inferred releases, private PyPI scope, npm channels, checksums, wrapper bump severity, provenance | Owner decisions; wire and public API changes are cheapest before 1.0 |\n| T12 | Production-path matrix: executed vs skipped vs simulated; real npm, Cargo and PyPI | Credentials; where the credential check runs |\n| T12-DX | Fresh-repo init-to-first-publish under 10 minutes, measured | T12 and credentials |\n| 1.0 | Accept ADR 12, refresh docs, decide which crates reach 1.0 (only `callisto-cli` is user-facing; libraries may stay 0.x), retired-crate notices (parked) | Owner decisions |\n\n## Open PRs from the 2026-10-20 review (all hosted CI green)\n\n| Stack or PR | Contents |\n| --- | --- |\n| #251 + #268 (stack 269) | Maturin after v1 and E007; record the D01 decisions in ADR 12 and the plan |\n| #252, #253, #255, #256, #257 (stack 254) | Tag ownership by declared name (promoted, pre.json, bare packages), dual-package selection expands, product waits for plugin tag, dependent waits for its own distribution |\n| #258, #259, #261 (stack 260) | Redact token shapes, redact failed-command stderr, real-registry tests fail under CI (coverage job opts out) |\n| #262 | Spec and doc corrections (E267/E266, matrix envelope, lockfile, retry limit, napi, ADR 9 and 10 Accepted) |\n| #263 | Crate metadata inheritance, package excludes, drop unused deps |\n| #264 | Simple generated workflow serializes releases |\n| #265 | Poetry caret rewrite, one-minor ranges stay narrow |\n| #266 | Group naming one package twice is E250 |\n| #267 | `version` reports unknown changeset entries |\n\nWaiting on owner decisions (see V1-REVIEW-2026-10-20.md section D): local route binds HEAD (A2), pre mode on the managed route (A3), pre-cycle stale ranges and range hard stop (A4), foreign published version (A5), snapshots (A6), OIDC, library crates at 1.0, E176 detail carry, schemaVersion bump. Not started: T06 PRs 2 to 5, MSRV job and scheduled advisory scan, edition 2024, semver-checks in CI, fuzz targets, panic hygiene, T12a harness PRs.\n\n## Rules\n\n- Read `AGENTS.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, the matching `docs/architecture/` topic and `docs/adr/README.md` first.\n- One `just ci` at a time, as `env -u FORCE_COLOR just ci`; read the log's own `exit=` line. No parallel cargo builds in one checkout.\n- Prove behavior with the real tool; confirm new tests fail on the old behavior.\n- Stacked PRs are native GitHub stacks (`gh stack link`). No force pushes, no session links, one line per Markdown paragraph.\n- Worktree sessions: `/usr/bin/git`, plain commands, scripts written to the scratchpad.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d8a7b747-3137-44ef-b1ae-391289e9277d","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:11:05.846Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"{\"mergeCommit\":{\"oid\":\"44ab50f93d32cd3655558f14196fe9f09547c263\"},\"mergedAt\":\"2026-10-21T18:11:01Z\",\"state\":\"MERGED\"}\n404aea289 fix(version): report a changeset entry that names no package (#267)\nb813d422a fix(config): reject a group that names one package under two spellings (#266)\na9ba42fb4 fix(manifests): rewrite Poetry carets and keep one-minor Python ranges narrow (#265)\n# Next work after the nested-workspace stack\n\nBaseline: main `308d35a91` (#247). Local only, never PR it. Verified against the code on 2026-10-18; the earlier version of this file (written at 0.10.2) listed work that has since shipped.\n\n## Shipped since the 0.10.2 plan\n\n- W1 apply mixed-routing tests (`apply/tests.rs`, `a_manifest_written_through_both_routes_...`).\n- W2 SYS-RETRY: `incomplete_tagged_releases` observes every operation of packages tagged on HEAD (`release/local.rs`).\n- W3 PYFILES: per-file completeness, partial upload recovery, sealed file sets (#232, #233).\n- W5 R3 and SYS-BARRIER: `derive_release_inputs_with` is a staged pipeline; `OpIndex::tag_prerequisites` makes a dual owner's tag wait for both publishes.\n- W6 R5 and SYS-NAPI: init tests and templates are out of line; the matrix workflow derives napi builds from the intent.\n- W7 R1: `walk.rs::build` is staged (`discover`, `assign_identities`, `resolve_packages`, `build_edges`).\n- Cargo, npm, pnpm and uv workspaces below the repo root, strict reads, ignored-file preflight, shallow-clone guard, unreadable changelog (#241-#247).\n\n## In flight\n\n- #249 PYROUTES: `publish-url` on a `pypi` registry.\n- #250 docs: drop the shipped T09 and T09-ROUTES plan entries.\n\n## Still open and not blocked\n\n- W0 is done once #250 merges. Branch cleanup finished 2026-10-18: 61 merged branches and 11 worktrees removed. Kept on purpose: `docs/crate-consolidation-plan`, `fix/release-consistency`, `refactor/apply-pipeline`, `test/black-box-gaps`, `fix/pypi-per-file-completeness`, `fix/python-declaration-locators` (local commits not in their merged PR heads), `worktree-wave2-base` (3 commits, no upstream), local-only `backup/`, `fix/stack-*`, `pr/*`, `stack/*`, `work/*` branches, `docs/next-work-plan` (locked worktree) and `main` (62 behind).\n- T08 leftover: `link_publish_prerequisites` (`release/derive.rs`) makes a dependent wait on every publish of the dependency package, not only the distribution the edge touches. Over-serializes, never unsafe.\n\n## Blocked on owner decisions\n\n- D01 owner contract: options and leans are in `.claude/plans/D01-DECISIONS.md` (2026-10-20). All of D01 decided 2026-10-20 (A to E, see the Decided table in D01-DECISIONS.md); T06 is unblocked once ADR 12 and the plan record the choices. SYS-OWNER, SYS-DEMOTION and the pre.json alias drop are fixed (#230, #222). D (bare packages adopt bare tags by name, path-exists branch ignores the declared name) is an existing-contract repair under ADR 11, not blocked. ADR 12 stays Proposed until A to C land.\n- W1 real-service credential check: where it runs in CI.\n- W4 redacted provider output: allow-list shape and the persisted wire change.\n- W10: `RewriteKey` discriminator (public API) and Python dev-group tracking.\n- W11 verification (T12, T12-DX): needs credentials and an owner-approved run.\n- Inferred-only or manual version releases in managed CI (policy).\n- Accepted gap: the version-level PyPI read counts a partial file set as present. Callisto tags only after a confirmed complete publish, so only a hand-made tag can expose it.\n- A Cargo workspace nested under a root Cargo workspace is still decided by the root's `members` and `exclude` (agreed with Codex; not changed).\n\n## v1 critical path (2026-10-20; superseded by V1-REVIEW-2026-10-20.md, which adds 13 uncovered defects and 13 owner decisions)\n\nChecked on the real binary at main (0.11.0): exactly the 8 user commands, `publish`/`plan-publish`/`tag`/`filter-plan` gone, `init --yes --versioning ... --workflow` writes a 31-line workflow, `release --dry-run` works on any branch. The plan JSON after #251 is one serial chain: D01 -> T06 -> T06-HISTORY -> T08 -> T12 -> T12-DX.\n\n| Step | What is left | Needs |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| D01 | Decided (A to E). Record in ADR 12, polyglot-v1 and the plan, then T06 is unblocked | A docs PR |\n| Ownership repair (T06-HISTORY residue) | Bare packages adopt bare tags by name; path-exists branch ignores the declared name; pre.json bare key with no historical check | Nothing; existing contract under ADR 11 |\n| T06 | One owner-aware resolver, canonical emission, legacy boundary, 24 spec criteria and about 400 fixtures | B and C |\n| T08 | Package-granular selection, optional plugin barrier edge, `link_publish_prerequisites` over-serialization | E. Changes intent digests, so land before 1.0 |\n| Parallel, small | `GroupTable::from_groups` conflict check, receipt run_attempt wording, moon pin in `.prototools`, rustc target facts, explicit registry kind scope | Nothing except kind scope |\n| Parallel, decisions | W4 redacted provider stderr (persisted wire change), W10 `RewriteKey` and dev-group tracking (public API), managed-CI inferred releases, private PyPI scope, npm channels, checksums, wrapper bump severity, provenance | Owner decisions; wire and public API changes are cheapest before 1.0 |\n| T12 | Production-path matrix: executed vs skipped vs simulated; real npm, Cargo and PyPI | Credentials; where the credential check runs |\n| T12-DX | Fresh-repo init-to-first-publish under 10 minutes, measured | T12 and credentials |\n| 1.0 | Accept ADR 12, refresh docs, decide which crates reach 1.0 (only `callisto-cli` is user-facing; libraries may stay 0.x), retired-crate notices (parked) | Owner decisions |\n\n## Open PRs from the 2026-10-20 review (all hosted CI green)\n\n| Stack or PR | Contents |\n| --- | --- |\n| #251 + #268 (stack 269) | Maturin after v1 and E007; record the D01 decisions in ADR 12 and the plan |\n| #252, #253, #255, #256, #257 (stack 254) | Tag ownership by declared name (promoted, pre.json, bare packages), dual-package selection expands, product waits for plugin tag, dependent waits for its own distribution |\n| #258, #259, #261 (stack 260) | Redact token shapes, redact failed-command stderr, real-registry tests fail under CI (coverage job opts out) |\n| #262 | Spec and doc corrections (E267/E266, matrix envelope, lockfile, retry limit, napi, ADR 9 and 10 Accepted) |\n| #263 | Crate metadata inheritance, package excludes, drop unused deps |\n| #264 | Simple generated workflow serializes releases |\n| #265 | Poetry caret rewrite, one-minor ranges stay narrow |\n| #266 | Group naming one package twice is E250 |\n| #267 | `version` reports unknown changeset entries |\n\nWaiting on owner decisions (see V1-REVIEW-2026-10-20.md section D): local route binds HEAD (A2), pre mode on the managed route (A3), pre-cycle stale ranges and range hard stop (A4), foreign published version (A5), snapshots (A6), OIDC, library crates at 1.0, E176 detail carry, schemaVersion bump. Not started: T06 PRs 2 to 5, MSRV job and scheduled advisory scan, edition 2024, semver-checks in CI, fuzz targets, panic hygiene, T12a harness PRs.\n\n## Rules\n\n- Read `AGENTS.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, the matching `docs/architecture/` topic and `docs/adr/README.md` first.\n- One `just ci` at a time, as `env -u FORCE_COLOR just ci`; read the log's own `exit=` line. No parallel cargo builds in one checkout.\n- Prove behavior with the real tool; confirm new tests fail on the old behavior.\n- Stacked PRs are native GitHub stacks (`gh stack link`). No force pushes, no session links, one line per Markdown paragraph.\n- Worktree sessions: `/usr/bin/git`, plain commands, scripts written to the scratchpad.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"classifierBoundary":true,"serverClassifierContext":{