{"parentUuid":"04990ac8-8f1a-4db1-a08a-2026f7d050c1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFqHE9xBvMuVXoMKH4AP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 16 fix PRs plus #270 are merged, and the only open PR is #248, the automated release PR. I updated the local plan file `.claude/plans/NEXT-WORK.md`, which is git-excluded, to match.\n\n**Next, in order:**\n1. **T06 PR 3 (E317):** a bare package name in `callisto.toml` becomes an error with a fix-it. It breaks existing configs, including this repo's own. Your call is still open on whether to do this or keep bare names allowed in config.\n2. **T06 PRs 4 and 5:** canonical command-line arguments, then canonical emission. The report `schemaVersion` bump is decided in the second of these.\n3. **Work that needs no decision from you:**\n   - An MSRV CI job.\n   - Scheduled `cargo deny`.\n   - Cargo dependabot.\n   - semver-checks in CI.\n   - Fuzz targets for the manifest editors.\n   - Edition 2024.\n   - Panic hygiene.\n4. **T08, T12 and T12-DX:** these wait on credentials and your open decisions listed in section D of `V1-REVIEW-2026-10-20.md`.\n\n**My suggestion:** while you decide on E317, I start the work that needs no decision, beginning with the MSRV job, scheduled `cargo deny` and Cargo dependabot as one CI PR. I'll also fold the dead `resolve_human` deletion into the next T06 PR. Say go and I'll start.\n\nresult: Everything through PR #270 is merged and the local plan is updated; the next step is the E317 decision (bare names in config), or I start the decision-free CI work (MSRV, scheduled `cargo deny`, dependabot) in the meantime."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1354,"cache_read_input_tokens":86236,"output_tokens":572,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"servi