{"parentUuid":"628eefb4-3489-42ac-9ed0-0c87c3d03f44","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"127e6260-98ab-4e06-9352-e8746af46641","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M9wsSmame9WPPrzVsww3Fx","type":"tool_result","content":"13:- Use canonical slash-qualified distribution references for new exact inputs, authored and generated data; reject new bare and colon-form aliases. Native normalization belongs to the ecosystem.\n15:- Read existing bare/colon references only through a deliberate compatibility/migration boundary with established ownership. Preserve historical tag ownership without using display promotion as a release-identity change.\n25:- Keep collision-triggered bare/qualified identity everywhere: retains inference rules at every new consumer and lets unrelated workspace changes alter identity behavior.\n.claude/plans/D01-DECISIONS.md:76:| Changesets, `callisto add`, config groups and rules, `pre.json`, `matrix --package` | bare, `eco:name`, `eco/name` (prefix case-insensitive) | bare when unpromoted, slash when promoted |\n.claude/plans/D01-DECISIONS.md:127:Cause: the ownership fallback runs only when the package id is already prefixed (`tags.rs:184-192,210`), so a bare package finds `foo@*` by name alone. ADR 11 lists \"fall back to `{name}@` tags without an ownership check\" as a rejected option, so this is a defect against an accepted decision, not a new policy. A Callisto tag annotation carries only `Release {tag_name}` (reproduced), and ADR 9 says the annotation is not a contract. The committed decision at the tag commit does list the owners with native names, but only for release-PR-flow releases and at a configurable path.\n.claude/plans/D01-DECISIONS.md:135:| R5 never adopt bare tags automatically | refuse and ask | none | every promoted or demoted workspace needs config |\n22:    \"build-artifact\": {\"attestations\", \"id-token\"},\n333:            if level == \"write\" and scope in (\"id-token\", \"attestations\") and name not in OIDC_JOBS:\n580:        \"id-token on execute\": after(\"\\n  execute:\\n\", \"      attestations: read\\n\",\n581:            \"      attestations: read\\n      id-token: write\\n\"),","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d973b023-9ba6-41dc-8bfd-5e564dc309a0","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:18:11.822Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"13:- Use canonical slash-qualified distribution references for new exact inputs, authored and generated data; reject new bare and colon-form aliases. Native normalization belongs to the ecosystem.\n15:- Read existing bare/colon references only through a deliberate compatibility/migration boundary with established ownership. Preserve historical tag ownership without using display promotion as a release-identity change.\n25:- Keep collision-triggered bare/qualified identity everywhere: retains inference rules at every new consumer and lets unrelated workspace changes alter identity behavior.\n.claude/plans/D01-DECISIONS.md:76:| Changesets, `callisto add`, config groups and rules, `pre.json`, `matrix --package` | bare, `eco:name`, `eco/name` (prefix case-insensitive) | bare when unpromoted, slash when promoted |\n.claude/plans/D01-DECISIONS.md:127:Cause: the ownership fallback runs only when the package id is already prefixed (`tags.rs:184-192,210`), so a bare package finds `foo@*` by name alone. ADR 11 lists \"fall back to `{name}@` tags without an ownership check\" as a rejected option, so this is a defect against an accepted decision, not a new policy. A Callisto tag annotation carries only `Release {tag_name}` (reproduced), and ADR 9 says the annotation is not a contract. The committed decision at the tag commit does list the owners with native names, but only for release-PR-flow releases and at a configurable path.\n.claude/plans/D01-DECISIONS.md:135:| R5 never adopt bare tags automatically | refuse and ask | none | every promoted or demoted workspace needs config |\n22:    \"build-artifact\": {\"attestations\", \"id-token\"},\n333:            if level == \"write\" and scope in (\"id-token\", \"attestations\") and name not in OIDC_JOBS:\n580:        \"id-token on execute\": after(\"\\n  execute:\\n\", \"      attestations: read\\n\",\n581:            \"      attestations: read\\n      id-token: write\\n\"),","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"classifierBoundary":true,"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"310b91d0-d4e1-4d0f-b1a7-a07b2503433a","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/plans","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","branch":"stack/docs-v1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":3,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/plans","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"628eefb4-3489-42ac-9ed0-0c87c3d03f44","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"stack/docs-v1","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
