{"parentUuid":"b8c9fcff-3bd4-450f-a8d4-bcbcdeeb7eb1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFqq8WWn6Jo7W1LnVkyr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013WurXyguFkXVfcwi9hR9xh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/plans/DECISION-PROPOSALS-2026-10-21.md <<'EOF'\n# Proposals for the pending owner decisions (2026-10-21)\n\nLocal only, never PR it. Source: `V1-REVIEW-2026-10-20.md` section D and the A-series defects, checked against what merged since (#249 to #270). Confidence is mine, not verified on hosted GitHub or real registries.\n\nPrinciple: prefer the option that is additive later over the one that is a one-way door. Wire formats, dist-tags and tag formats are one-way doors; docs, warnings and new features are not.\n\n## Already decided or shipped (confirm only)\n\n| Item | State | Proposal |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| D6 dual package `--package` selection | #255 merged: selecting one distribution releases the whole package | Confirm; document in `releasing.md` |\n| D8 W4 redaction | #258, #259 merged (token shapes, stderr). Remaining: show a tail on E176 and E157 | Print-only redacted tail, 20 lines or 2 KiB, no persisted field (no wire change) |\n| E317 bare names in config | ADR 12 already says \"reject new bare and colon-form aliases\" | Do it: hard error with the exact `eco/name` fix-it, convert this repo's `callisto.toml` in the same PR |\n\n## Decisions with a recommendation\n\n| # | Decision | Recommend | Why | Reversible? |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | OIDC trusted publishing | Keep tokens for 1.0 and document it. Post-1.0: opt-in OIDC in generated workflows and `execute` | Needs a policy-script change, first publish on crates.io and npm is manual anyway, and tokens are already confined to `execute`. Additive later | Yes |\n| 2 | Crates at 1.0 | Only `callisto-cli` at 1.0. Libraries stay 0.x and documented unstable; split them out of the fixed group | About 1,050 `pub` items, no semver-checks, `non_exhaustive` uneven. A fixed group forces a CLI major on any library break | Yes (promote later) |\n| 3 | Pre mode on the managed route | Local-only for 1.0. Fix the defect regardless: `version` in pre mode with no changeset must be a no-op (no beta.N churn) and the managed route must fail early with one clear error | Supporting it needs a new verification rule; prereleases are rare in managed CI | Yes |\n| 4 | Snapshots | Never tag or publish a snapshot; `release` refuses a snapshot version | Adding a publish path later is additive; removing one is not. Also removes the dist-tag question for snapshots | Yes |\n| 5 | Dist-tag | Derive from the pre identifier (`1.0.0-beta.1` -> `beta`); fall back to `next`; never `latest` for a prerelease | `next` for beta and rc misleads installers. Changing it later moves what users install | No, decide now |\n| 7 | T06 wire shape | Yes to all four: `schemaVersion` 2 on the four reports (canonical ids in keys), package-set globs as `eco/glob` (matches E316), text tables show canonical ids, `add` keeps native names in changesets (ADR 12) | Changing keys without a bump is silent breakage; pre-1.0 is the cheapest window. Ship the four together as one breaking changeset | No, decide now |\n| 9 | Managed-CI inferred-only releases | Changesets are the sole input in managed CI; `status --check` flags pending-without-changeset for `auto` packages | Avoids an ADR 2 revision; the flag is a CI-visible safety net | Yes |\n| 10 | Provenance | Add the bot-author check if it is not an approval gate under the owner policy (verify against `verify-release-workflow-policy.sh` first); else accept and document | One jq clause, cheap | Yes |\n| 11 | Python dev tables | Document-only for 1.0, but make the skip loud (warning naming the file). Group tracking changes public API (`RewriteKey`) | We do not need the API change to ship 1.0 | Yes |\n| 12 | `@v1`, platforms, 10-minute claim | Publish immutable `vX.Y.Z` plus a floating `v1`; generated workflows use `@v1`, docs show SHA pinning. Add x86_64-apple and aarch64-linux; Windows is documented unsupported until it has CI. Drop the \"under 10 minutes\" number from user copy until T12-DX measures it | Claiming Windows without CI is worse than not claiming it | Yes |\n| 13 | T12b credentials | Owner-run local script against scratch registries first (`just verify-real`), local registries (verdaccio, devpi) for the bulk. A hosted workflow with secrets violates the enforced policy, so defer it | Zero policy impact; reproducible evidence | Yes |\n\n## A-series repairs that were \"waiting on decisions\"\n\n| Defect | Proposal |\n| --- | --- |\n| A2 local route releases HEAD | Bind the tag and publish to the commit that introduced the version; refuse otherwise with an error whose fix is `git checkout <sha>`. Add a `concurrency:` group to the generated simple workflow now (no decision needed). Needs a short design spike for the mechanism (low confidence on the exact rule) |\n| A3 pre mode managed | See decision 3 |\n| A4 stale ranges after a pre cycle | Rewrite dependents' `^X-pre` ranges when the dependency graduates. Unrepresentable peer or compound ranges become a hard error before any write (today: warning, or half-applied then E208 and E121 on rerun) |\n| A5 foreign published version | Keep adopting an exact published version (ADR 3). Fix the tag target via A2. Warn, not block, when registry repository metadata does not match the origin remote |\n| A6 snapshots | See decision 4 |\n\n## Suggested order\n\n1. Decide the one-way doors now: 5, 7, and the E317 go-ahead.\n2. Start without further decisions: CI hygiene PR (MSRV, scheduled `cargo deny`, Cargo dependabot, semver-checks), generated-workflow `concurrency:`, pre-mode no-op fix, pre-write range hard stop.\n3. T06 PRs 3 to 5 once 7 is confirmed.\n4. A2 spike, then T08, then T12 with the local script.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Save decision proposals to local plans"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2965,"cache_read_input_tokens":100539,"output_tokens":2472,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":184},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2965,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2472,"cache_read_input_tokens":100539,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2965,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2965},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013WurXyguFkXVfcwi9hR9xh":{"command":"cat > /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/plans/DECISION-PROPOSALS-2026-10-21.md <<'EOF'\n# Proposals for the pending owner decisions (2026-10-21)\n\nLocal only, never PR it. Source: `V1-REVIEW-2026-10-20.md` section D and the A-series defects, checked against what merged since (#249 to #270). Confidence is mine, not verified on hosted GitHub or real registries.\n\nPrinciple: prefer the option that is additive later over the one that is a one-way door. Wire formats, dist-tags and tag formats are one-way doors; docs, warnings and new features are not.\n\n## Already decided or shipped (confirm only)\n\n| Item | State | Proposal |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| D6 dual package `--package` selection | #255 merged: selecting one distribution releases the whole package | Confirm; document in `releasing.md` |\n| D8 W4 redaction | #258, #259 merged (token shapes, stderr). Remaining: show a tail on E176 and E157 | Print-only redacted tail, 20 lines or 2 KiB, no persisted field (no wire change) |\n| E317 bare names in config | ADR 12 already says \"reject new bare and colon-form aliases\" | Do it: hard error with the exact `eco/name` fix-it, convert this repo's `callisto.toml` in the same PR |\n\n## Decisions with a recommendation\n\n| # | Decision | Recommend | Why | Reversible? |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | OIDC trusted publishing | Keep tokens for 1.0 and document it. Post-1.0: opt-in OIDC in generated workflows and `execute` | Needs a policy-script change, first publish on crates.io and npm is manual anyway, and tokens are already confined to `execute`. Additive later | Yes |\n| 2 | Crates at 1.0 | Only `callisto-cli` at 1.0. Libraries stay 0.x and documented unstable; split them out of the fixed group | About 1,050 `pub` items, no semver-checks, `non_exhaustive` uneven. A fixed group forces a CLI major on any library break | Yes (promote later) |\n| 3 | Pre mode on the managed route | Local-only for 1.0. Fix the defect regardless: `version` in pre mode with no changeset must be a no-op (no beta.N churn) and the managed route must fail early with one clear error | Supporting it needs a new verification rule; prereleases are rare in managed CI | Yes |\n| 4 | Snapshots | Never tag or publish a snapshot; `release` refuses a snapshot version | Adding a publish path later is additive; removing one is not. Also removes the dist-tag question for snapshots | Yes |\n| 5 | Dist-tag | Derive from the pre identifier (`1.0.0-beta.1` -> `beta`); fall back to `next`; never `latest` for a prerelease | `next` for beta and rc misleads installers. Changing it later moves what users install | No, decide now |\n| 7 | T06 wire shape | Yes to all four: `schemaVersion` 2 on the four reports (canonical ids in keys), package-set globs as `eco/glob` (matches E316), text tables show canonical ids, `add` keeps native names in changesets (ADR 12) | Changing keys without a bump is silent breakage; pre-1.0 is the cheapest window. Ship the four together as one breaking changeset | No, decide now |\n| 9 | Managed-CI inferred-only releases | Changesets are the sole input in managed CI; `status --check` flags pending-without-changeset for `auto` packages | Avoids an ADR 2 revision; the flag is a CI-visible safety net | Yes |\n| 10 | Provenance | Add the bot-author check if it is not an approval gate under the owner policy (verify against `verify-release-workflow-policy.sh` first); else accept and document | One jq clause, cheap | Yes |\n| 11 | Python dev tables | Document-only for 1.0, but make the skip loud (warning naming the file). Group tracking changes public API (`RewriteKey`) | We do not need the API change to ship 1.0 | Yes |\n| 12 | `@v1`, platforms, 10-minute claim | Publish immutable `vX.Y.Z` plus a floating `v1`; generated workflows use `@v1`, docs show SHA pinning. Add x86_64-apple and aarch64-linux; Windows is documented unsupported until it has CI. Drop the \"under 10 minutes\" number from user copy until T12-DX measures it | Claiming Windows without CI is worse than not claiming it | Yes |\n| 13 | T12b credentials | Owner-run local script against scratch registries first (`just verify-real`), local registries (verdaccio, devpi) for the bulk. A hosted workflow with secrets violates the enforced policy, so defer it | Zero policy impact; reproducible evidence | Yes |\n\n## A-series repairs that were \"waiting on decisions\"\n\n| Defect | Proposal |\n| --- | --- |\n| A2 local route releases HEAD | Bind the tag and publish to the commit that introduced the version; refuse otherwise with an error whose fix is `git checkout <sha>`. Add a `concurrency:` group to the generated simple workflow now (no decision needed). Needs a short design spike for the mechanism (low confidence on the exact rule) |\n| A3 pre mode managed | See decision 3 |\n| A4 stale ranges after a pre cycle | Rewrite dependents' `^X-pre` ranges when the dependency graduates. Unrepresentable peer or compound ranges become a hard error before any write (today: warning, or half-applied then E208 and E121 on rerun) |\n| A5 foreign published version | Keep adopting an exact published version (ADR 3). Fix the tag target via A2. Warn, not block, when registry repository metadata does not match the origin remote |\n| A6 snapshots | See decision 4 |\n\n## Suggested order\n\n1. Decide the one-way doors now: 5, 7, and the E317 go-ahead.\n2. Start without further decisions: CI hygiene PR (MSRV, scheduled `cargo deny`, Cargo dependabot, semver-checks), generated-workflow `concurrency:`, pre-mode no-op fix, pre-write range hard stop.\n3. T06 PRs 3 to 5 once 7 is confirmed.\n4. A2 spike, then T08, then T12 with the local script.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Save decision proposals to local plans"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"6804ba34-4eef-45cd-9c7a-5ac81a181700","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgFqq8EQ4h7GupKaxgAJC","requestRef":"8c9702a4-af6f-4c18-8726-29e63a955cd4","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"85b8beac-1113-409f-b811-5cae8af4b9d4","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:18:44.857Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"stack/docs-v1","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
