{"parentUuid":"c02cb8fb-851d-4e18-9a17-8080b507034c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_014xh2XL3zjucvFkFqFyTVE1","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5b5c8499-591a-4ca1-bdb0-bd2186f24ec8","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:22:56.443Z","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"stack/docs-v1","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"5b5c8499-591a-4ca1-bdb0-bd2186f24ec8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFrADnoJiw4y8KKoFybu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Lockstep it is for callisto. It already is lockstep, so the plan only changes in one place.\n\nThe michi branch `refactor/michi-core-merge` fits what you said. Its `main` just hasn't caught up yet, which is why the repo still looked independent when I checked.\n\n**Callisto's current state:**\n- **Versioning:** all five crates are already in one fixed group in `callisto.toml`, so they already version in lockstep.\n- **Crate count:** the consolidation to four published crates already shipped in #157. The four are `callisto-model`, `callisto-manifests`, `callisto-graph` and `callisto-cli`. The fifth, `callisto-fixtures`, is dev-only. The old `docs/crate-consolidation-plan` branch is stale, so I'll delete it.\n- **Further merging:** `callisto-model` has to stay a separate crate because it is MIT and the others are FSL. Merging `callisto-manifests` into `callisto-graph` is possible, but I'd leave it for after 1.0. It doesn't affect the 1.0 contract.\n\n**What changes in the plan:** decision 2 becomes \"all four published crates go to 1.0 together.\" The libraries get an \"internal implementation, no API stability guarantee\" note, so a library change doesn't force a CLI major version. `cargo-semver-checks` then applies only to what we choose to promise. I'd start with `callisto-cli`'s `schema` output and its config and report formats, not the `pub` Rust items. That also drops the \"split the libraries out of the fixed group\" step, because no split is needed.\n\nI'll update the plan notes and then start the CI hygiene PR.\n\nresult: Decision 2 is now lockstep: all four published callisto crates go to 1.0 together, and the libraries are marked internal with no API guarantee. The crate consolidation already shipped in #157, so no split is needed, and I start the CI hygiene PR next."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":547,"cache_read_input_tokens":115742,"output_tokens":630,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":547,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":630,"cache_read_input_tokens":115742,"cache_creation_input_tokens":547,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":547},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"4854757f-22ec-4932-a689-dcf26db78136","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFrADThXYM7qgUNsWMM8","requestRef":"88dc284a-1668-47db-adaa-c978b3114e89","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c23e3a2b-dc7a-4618-889c-9812f2ad99e8","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:22:56.443Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"stack/docs-v1","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
