{"parentUuid":"6014a3f1-cca2-41aa-a3ce-0ec903cc39cf","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f5cf9b4b-3262-4a4b-a98f-8654c9cfb941","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012NbFYqMgYRQ5FB9RCwVBsj","type":"tool_result","content":"./docs/projects/V1-SYSTEM-HARDENING.json:45:        \"Implement ADR 12's canonical-reference contract with one owner-aware resolver: canonical required in config, groups, rules, product and artifact packages, report and matrix keys and CLI arguments; colon rejected with a code that names the slash form (E316); a bare reference in config rejected with a fix-it (E317). Changesets and pre.json keep native names resolved at read time, with a hard error for colon. Platform-manifest npm names in groups stay native. Do not change tag names.\",\n| E309 | `release build-python` run with `--dry-run`, which cannot write build output | re-run `callisto release build-python` without --dry-run |\n| E310 | Failed to read manifest `<path>`: <message> | Make the manifest readable UTF-8 text; a workspace member's manifest is never skipped. |\n| E311 | Invalid workspace membership in `<path>`: <message> | Make `members`/`exclude` (Cargo, uv) or `workspaces`/`packages` (npm, pnpm) an array of valid glob strings; Callisto will not guess which packages a malforme\n| E312 | Package `<path>` is reached through a symbolic link, which Git cannot stage | Replace the link with the real directory, or list it in a .gitignore under the workspace root so discovery skips it; Callisto cannot \n| E313 | The workspace is incomplete: N manifest(s) could not be resolved | Fix or remove the manifests named above and re-run; Callisto will not plan a release from a partial workspace. |\n| E314 | Cannot apply the version plan: N file(s) cannot be written, so nothing was changed | Fix the files named above (a missing file, permissions, a symbolic link Git cannot stage, or a path a .gitignore ignores) and \n| E315 | Commit-based version inference needs the full Git history, but this repository is a shallow clone | Fetch the full history (`git fetch --unshallow`, or `fetch-depth: 0` for actions/checkout), or give the package\n| E316 | A package reference uses the colon form (`cargo:foo`) | Write the slash form the message names (`cargo/foo`); it is the only qualified spelling in `callisto.toml`, changesets, `pre.json` and command-line argumen\n\n\n241 numeric E#### codes total in one registry.\n284:| E241 | `init --yes` is missing required flag(s) | supply the listed flags; see `callisto init --help` |\n315:241 numeric E#### codes total in one registry.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"817ea0f5-15bd-4a41-bc79-cbc76661ae6e","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:01:13.250Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"./docs/projects/V1-SYSTEM-HARDENING.json:45:        \"Implement ADR 12's canonical-reference contract with one owner-aware resolver: canonical required in config, groups, rules, product and artifact packages, report and matrix keys and CLI arguments; colon rejected with a code that names the slash form (E316); a bare reference in config rejected with a fix-it (E317). Changesets and pre.json keep native names resolved at read time, with a hard error for colon. Platform-manifest npm names in groups stay native. Do not change tag names.\",\n| E309 | `release build-python` run with `--dry-run`, which cannot write build output | re-run `callisto release build-python` without --dry-run |\n| E310 | Failed to read manifest `<path>`: <message> | Make the manifest readable UTF-8 text; a workspace member's manifest is never skipped. |\n| E311 | Invalid workspace membership in `<path>`: <message> | Make `members`/`exclude` (Cargo, uv) or `workspaces`/`packages` (npm, pnpm) an array of valid glob strings; Callisto will not guess which packages a malforme\n| E312 | Package `<path>` is reached through a symbolic link, which Git cannot stage | Replace the link with the real directory, or list it in a .gitignore under the workspace root so discovery skips it; Callisto cannot \n| E313 | The workspace is incomplete: N manifest(s) could not be resolved | Fix or remove the manifests named above and re-run; Callisto will not plan a release from a partial workspace. |\n| E314 | Cannot apply the version plan: N file(s) cannot be written, so nothing was changed | Fix the files named above (a missing file, permissions, a symbolic link Git cannot stage, or a path a .gitignore ignores) and \n| E315 | Commit-based version inference needs the full Git history, but this repository is a shallow clone | Fetch the full history (`git fetch --unshallow`, or `fetch-depth: 0` for actions/checkout), or give the package\n| E316 | A package reference uses the colon form (`cargo:foo`) | Write the slash form the message names (`cargo/foo`); it is the only qualified spelling in `callisto.toml`, changesets, `pre.json` and command-line argumen\n\n\n241 numeric E#### codes total in one registry.\n284:| E241 | `init --yes` is missing required flag(s) | supply the listed flags; see `callisto init --help` |\n315:241 numeric E#### codes total in one registry.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"classifierBoundary":true,"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"36b863bd-0910-48bb-b5d7-e49724ac2603","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-canonical-config","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-canonical-config","branch":"worktree-t06-canonical-config","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claud