{"parentUuid":"eeb6f8ce-8abb-402e-ac09-8999c4b18642","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f5cf9b4b-3262-4a4b-a98f-8654c9cfb941","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DYWfYmcJmzN6ng6MbN65jP","type":"tool_result","content":"# callisto configuration\n\n[[fixed-group]]\nname = \"workspace\"\nmembers = [\n    \"callisto-model\",\n    \"callisto-manifests\",\n    \"callisto-graph\",\n    \"callisto-cli\",\n    \"callisto-fixtures\",\n]\n\n[changesets]\ndir = \".changeset\"\nkind = \"npm\"\nurl = \"https://npm.internal.example.com\"\n```\n\n## `[[package]]` and `[[package-set]]`\n\nBoth blocks share five override fields, parsed identically; `[[package]]` also accepts `previous-tag-templates`. `[[package]]`'s `match` is an exact `PackageId` (first matching rule wins, prefixed forms like `cargo/foo` take priority over bare `foo` regardless of declaration order). `[[package-set]]`'s `match` is a glob `PackagePattern` and can match many packages at once; `[[package]]` always takes priority over `[[package-set]]` for a given package.\n\n| Key | Type | Default | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `match` | string | required | `[[package]]`: exact ecosystem-qualified id or bare name. `[[package-set]]`: glob pattern. |\n| `release-trigger` | string (`\"changeset\"` \\| `\"auto\"`) | none — every field here is an `Option`; omitted means \"use this package's own default\", not a config-level default | What causes this package to be considered for release |\n| `publish-to` | array of strings (`\"crates-io\"` \\| `\"npm\"` \\| `\"pypi\"` \\| `\"nuget\"` \\| `\"github-release\"` \\| `\"none\"`) | none | Where this package publishes |\n| `tag-template` | string | none | Git tag template, e.g. `\"callisto@{version}\"` |\n| `previous-tag-templates` | array of strings | `[]` | `[[package]]` only (`[[package-set]]` rejects it). Earlier tag templates checked (in order) for this package's last release tag, only if `tag-template` finds none. They are matched by name only, so this is how a renamed package claims the tags it made under its old name |\n| `changelog` | string | none | Changelog path, relative to the package's own root. Forward-slash-separated only; rejected if absolute or containing `..` (E113). |\n| `pre-major-inference` | string (`\"off\"` \\| `\"conservative\"` \\| `\"conservative-feat\"`) | `\"off\"` | Pre-1.0 severity-downgrade policy: `conservative` downgrades an inferred Major to Minor; `conservative-feat` also downgrades Minor to Patch |\n\nExample (this repo's own `callisto.toml`):\n```toml\n[[package]]\nmatch = \"cargo/callisto-cli\"\npublish-to = [\"crates-io\", \"github-release\"]\ntag-template = \"callisto@{version}\"\nprevious-tag-templates = [\"callisto-cli@{version}\"]\n```\n\n## `[[fixed-group]]` and `[[linked-group]]`\n\nNeither has a config-level default for its fields — both are required when the block is present.\n\n| Key | Type | Required | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `name` | string | yes | Group identifier, unique across both fixed and linked groups |\n| `members` | array of strings | yes, non-empty | Package names in the group |\n\n`[[fixed-group]]`: all members bump in lock-step from the group's alignment base. `[[linked-group]]`: every member receives the highest severity and aligns to the highest target version produced by the members' bumps. Both currently require compatible version grammars; neither is an automatic cross-language version converter.\n\nExample (this repo's own `callisto.toml`):\n```toml\n[[fixed-group]]\nname = \"workspace\"\nmembers = [\"callisto-model\", \"callisto-manifests\", \"callisto-graph\", \"callisto-cli\"]\n```\n\n## `[init]`\n\nDeprecated. `ecosystems` (array of strings) is parsed so older config files still load, but nothing reads it.\n\n## Identity and defaults\n\nUnspecified package fields are filled during graph construction: the release trigger defaults to changesets, the changelog to the package directory, and publish targets to those declared by its manifests. Default tags use the display id, so newly created tags become qualified after name promotion; historical bare tags use the ownership fallback described in [identity](architecture/identity.md). Canonical references alone do not repair the open rename/demotion failures.\n      \"error_conditions\": [\n        \"A bare name shared by promoted packages is E103; a qualified name with no such manifest is E102.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"[[package]] match\",\n      \"signature\": \"match = \\\"<name>\\\" | \\\"<ecosystem>/<name>\\\"\",\n      \"description\": \"Exact package id. Ecosystem prefixes: cargo, npm, pypi.\",\n      \"error_conditions\": [\n        \"An empty, absolute, `..`-containing or otherwise unparseable id fails config loading.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"[[package-set]] match\",\n      \"signature\": \"match = \\\"<glob>\\\" | \\\"<ecosystem>/<glob>\\\"\",\n      \"description\": \"Glob over package names. The slash form scopes the glob to an ecosystem; a bare glob matches any ecosystem.\",\n      \"error_conditions\": [\n        \"An invalid glob fails config loading.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-DISC-01\",\n      \"criterion\": \"Root detection walks up from the start directory, never past the Git toplevel, and picks the nearest directory with a workspace marker (Cargo.toml with a `workspace` table, package.json with `workspaces`, pnpm-workspace.yaml, or a .moon directory); with no marker it picks the outermost directory with a package manifest (Cargo.toml with a `package` table, package.json, or pyproject.toml). A Cargo `workspace` or `package` table counts however it is written: a header, an inline table, dotted keys, or, for `workspace`, a sub-table such as `[workspace.package]` alone.\"","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"28d02174-e00d-4684-ab2b-36c8def8d490","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:08:54.450Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# callisto configuration\n\n[[fixed-group]]\nname = \"workspace\"\nmembers = [\n    \"callisto-model\",\n    \"callisto-manifests\",\n    \"callisto-graph\",\n    \"callisto-cli\",\n    \"callisto-fixtures\",\n]\n\n[changesets]\ndir = \".changeset\"\nkind = \"npm\"\nurl = \"https://npm.internal.example.com\"\n```\n\n## `[[package]]` and `[[package-set]]`\n\nBoth blocks share five override fields, parsed identically; `[[package]]` also accepts `previous-tag-templates`. `[[package]]`'s `match` is an exact `PackageId` (first matching rule wins, prefixed forms like `cargo/foo` take priority over bare `foo` regardless of declaration order). `[[package-set]]`'s `match` is a glob `PackagePattern` and can match many packages at once; `[[package]]` always takes priority over `[[package-set]]` for a given package.\n\n| Key | Type | Default | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `match` | string | required | `[[package]]`: exact ecosystem-qualified id or bare name. `[[package-set]]`: glob pattern. |\n| `release-trigger` | string (`\"changeset\"` \\| `\"auto\"`) | none — every field here is an `Option`; omitted means \"use this package's own default\", not a config-level default | What causes this package to be considered for release |\n| `publish-to` | array of strings (`\"crates-io\"` \\| `\"npm\"` \\| `\"pypi\"` \\| `\"nuget\"` \\| `\"github-release\"` \\| `\"none\"`) | none | Where this package publishes |\n| `tag-template` | string | none | Git tag template, e.g. `\"callisto@{version}\"` |\n| `previous-tag-templates` | array of strings | `[]` | `[[package]]` only (`[[package-set]]` rejects it). Earlier tag templates checked (in order) for this package's last release tag, only if `tag-template` finds none. They are matched by name only, so this is how a renamed package claims the tags it made under its old name |\n| `changelog` | string | none | Changelog path, relative to the package's own root. Forward-slash-separated only; rejected if absolute or containing `..` (E113). |\n| `pre-major-inference` | string (`\"off\"` \\| `\"conservative\"` \\| `\"conservative-feat\"`) | `\"off\"` | Pre-1.0 severity-downgrade policy: `conservative` downgrades an inferred Major to Minor; `conservative-feat` also downgrades Minor to Patch |\n\nExample (this repo's own `callisto.toml`):\n```toml\n[[package]]\nmatch = \"cargo/callisto-cli\"\npublish-to = [\"crates-io\", \"github-release\"]\ntag-template = \"callisto@{version}\"\nprevious-tag-templates = [\"callisto-cli@{version}\"]\n```\n\n## `[[fixed-group]]` and `[[linked-group]]`\n\nNeither has a config-level default for its fields — both are required when the block is present.\n\n| Key | Type | Required | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `name` | string | yes | Group identifier, unique across both fixed and linked groups |\n| `members` | array of strings | yes, non-empty | Package names in the group |\n\n`[[fixed-group]]`: all members bump in lock-step from the group's alignment base. `[[linked-group]]`: every member receives the highest severity and aligns to the highest target version produced by the members' bumps. Both currently require compatible version grammars; neither is an automatic cross-language version converter.\n\nExample (this repo's own `callisto.toml`):\n```toml\n[[fixed-group]]\nname = \"workspace\"\nmembers = [\"callisto-model\", \"callisto-manifests\", \"callisto-graph\", \"callisto-cli\"]\n```\n\n## `[init]`\n\nDeprecated. `ecosystems` (array of strings) is parsed so older config files still load, but nothing reads it.\n\n## Identity and defaults\n\nUnspecified package fields are filled during graph construction: the release trigger defaults to changesets, the changelog to the package directory, and publish targets to those declared by its manifests. Default tags use the display id, so newly created tags become qualified after name promotion; historical bare tags use the ownership fallback described in [identity](architecture/identity.md). Canonical references alone do not repair the open rename/demotion failures.\n      \"error_conditions\": [\n        \"A bare name shared by promoted packages is E103; a qualified name with no such manifest is E102.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"[[package]] match\",\n      \"signature\": \"match = \\\"<name>\\\" | \\\"<ecosystem>/<name>\\\"\",\n      \"description\": \"Exact package id. Ecosystem prefixes: cargo, npm, pypi.\",\n      \"error_conditions\": [\n        \"An empty, absolute, `..`-containing or otherwise unparseable id fails config loading.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"[[package-set]] match\",\n      \"signature\": \"match = \\\"<glob>\\\" | \\\"<ecosystem>/<glob>\\\"\",\n      \"description\": \"Glob over package names. The slash form scopes the glob to an ecosystem; a bare glob matches any ecosystem.\",\n      \"error_conditions\": [\n        \"An invalid glob fails config loading.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-DISC-01\",\n      \"criterion\": \"Root detection walks up from the start directory, never past the Git toplevel, and picks the nearest directory with a workspace marker (Cargo.toml with a `workspace` table, package.json with `workspaces`, pnpm-workspace.yaml, or a .moon directory); with no marker it picks the outermost directory with a package manifest (Cargo.toml with a `package` table, package.json, or pyproject.toml). A Cargo `workspace` or `package` table counts however it is written: a header, an inline table, dotted keys, or, for `workspace`, a sub-table such as `[workspace.package]` alone.\"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"82c8e461-d992-4838-9410-462c527c15e5","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-canonical-config","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-canonical-config","branch":"worktree-t06-canonical-config","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"