{"parentUuid":"ba99c11e-57ee-4ac6-a44b-16ffadc99017","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f5cf9b4b-3262-4a4b-a98f-8654c9cfb941","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014NPBLKBchuNWH6NXD8vNSx","type":"tool_result","content":"    \"Fixed and linked group semantics other than naming a platform package as a member.\",\n    \"Ecosystems other than Cargo, npm and Python.\"\n  ],\n  \"api_surface\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Package key\",\n      \"signature\": \"Package::key() -> Option<PackageKey>\",\n      \"description\": \"A package's stable internal identity: the workspace-relative directory of its first canonical manifest. Promotion never changes it. Never printed as a package id.\",\n      \"error_conditions\": [\n        \"`None` only for a package with no canonical manifest, which workspace loading never produces.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Package id\",\n      \"signature\": \"PackageId = \\\"<name>\\\" | \\\"<ecosystem>/<name>\\\"\",\n      \"description\": \"Display and selector form: the bare manifest name, or `<ecosystem>/<name>` once another ecosystem declares the same name. JSON output, messages, changeset entries and `pre.json` keys use it; `<ecosystem>/<name>` selects the package whether or not it is promoted.\",\n      \"error_conditions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-ID-12\",\n      \"criterion\": \"A package reference written in the colon form (`cargo:foo`) is rejected with E316 naming the slash form (`cargo/foo`) wherever a package is named: `--package` on `add`, `matrix` and `release`, changeset entries, `pre.json` keys, group members, `[[package]]` and `[[package-set]]` `match`, `product-package` and `[[release.artifact]] package`. A bare name and the slash form are unaffected.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    },\ndocs/specs/workspace.json:23:      \"description\": \"Display and selector form: the bare manifest name, or `<ecosystem>/<name>` once another ecosystem declares the same name. JSON output, messages, changeset entries and `pre.json` keys use it; `<ecosystem>/<name\ndocs/specs/workspace.json:25:        \"A bare name shared by promoted packages is E103; a qualified name with no such manifest is E102.\"\ndocs/specs/workspace.json:39:      \"description\": \"Glob over package names. The slash form scopes the glob to an ecosystem; a bare glob matches any ecosystem.\",\ndocs/specs/workspace.json:111:      \"criterion\": \"A package whose name is claimed by no other directory gets a bare id equal to its manifest name (for example `foo` or `@scope/foo`).\"\ndocs/specs/workspace.json:119:      \"criterion\": \"When two or more directories declare the same name and no ecosystem declares it in more than one of them, each package is promoted to an ecosystem-qualified id, displayed as `cargo/foo`. Promotion preserves the\ndocs/specs/workspace.json:128:      \"criterion\": \"A `[[fixed-group]]` or `[[linked-group]]` member written `cargo/foo` resolves to package `foo` when a Cargo manifest declares `foo`, promoted or not, through the same selector resolver used for `--package` and \ndocs/specs/workspace.json:133:      \"criterion\": \"A changeset, `callisto add --package` or `callisto matrix --package` naming the bare name of promoted packages fails with E103 listing every qualified candidate and showing the qualified form to write; naming a\ndocs/specs/workspace.json:151:      \"criterion\": \"A package reference written in the colon form (`cargo:foo`) is rejected with E316 naming the slash form (`cargo/foo`) wherever a package is named: `--package` on `add`, `matrix` and `release`, changeset entries\ndocs/specs/workspace.json:166:      \"criterion\": \"For each package, the first ecosystem-prefixed `[[package]]` rule whose ecosystem the package actually has a manifest in and whose name matches applies, regardless of declaration order relative to bare rules; a\ndocs/specs/workspace.json:170:      \"criterion\": \"A bare `[[package]]` rule that would apply to a promoted package fails loading with E103 listing the qualified candidates; prefixed rules for the same packages load normally.\",\ndocs/specs/workspace.json:193:      \"criterion\": \"A bare `[[package]]` rule matching packages whose manifests span two or more ecosystems, such as a dual-manifest package, emits one non-fatal `bare-rule-matches-multiple-ecosystems` warning; prefixed rules and \ndocs/architecture/identity.md:3:How the workspace names packages, why bare names match across ecosystems, and where platform packages are wired in. Behavior: [`docs/specs/workspace.json`](../specs/workspace.json). Config keys: [`docs/config.md`](../config.md).\ndocs/architecture/identity.md:18:- `parse` treats text before the first `/` as a prefix only when `Ecosystem::from_prefix` knows it, so `@scope/foo` stays bare. It still reads `cargo:foo`; every user-facing input rejects that form with E316 first.\ndocs/architecture/identity.md:21:- Default tags use `display_name()`: `foo@{version}` while bare, `cargo/foo@{version}` after promotion. Promotion therefore also changes the namespace of newly created default tags (ADR 11).\ndocs/architecture/identity.md:24:  - A bare id matches any id with the same name, in either direction: bare is an ecosystem wildcard.\ndocs/architecture/identity.md:32:- `aggregate::resolve_target_package` resolves changeset entries through `IdentityIndex::resolve_id`, which maps qualified native distribution names to their owner and rejects ambiguous bare names. `status` attributes changeset\ndocs/architecture/identity.md:33:- `[[package]]` rules use `config::resolve::resolve_package_config`: two linear passes over the rules in declaration order, prefixed rules first, then bare. It never sorts the rules. A bare rule that reaches a promoted name is \ndocs/architecture/identity.md:51:For a promoted package, `TagIndex::build` also considers bare-name tags. `history::sole_owner_at` picks the same-named candidate whose first canonical manifest path held a manifest declaring the name at the tag's commit. When n","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5552a214-32aa-4661-9e5e-af048750d34e","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:08:58.647Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"    \"Fixed and linked group semantics other than naming a platform package as a member.\",\n    \"Ecosystems other than Cargo, npm and Python.\"\n  ],\n  \"api_surface\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Package key\",\n      \"signature\": \"Package::key() -> Option<PackageKey>\",\n      \"description\": \"A package's stable internal identity: the workspace-relative directory of its first canonical manifest. Promotion never changes it. Never printed as a package id.\",\n      \"error_conditions\": [\n        \"`None` only for a package with no canonical manifest, which workspace loading never produces.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Package id\",\n      \"signature\": \"PackageId = \\\"<name>\\\" | \\\"<ecosystem>/<name>\\\"\",\n      \"description\": \"Display and selector form: the bare manifest name, or `<ecosystem>/<name>` once another ecosystem declares the same name. JSON output, messages, changeset entries and `pre.json` keys use it; `<ecosystem>/<name>` selects the package whether or not it is promoted.\",\n      \"error_conditions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-ID-12\",\n      \"criterion\": \"A package reference written in the colon form (`cargo:foo`) is rejected with E316 naming the slash form (`cargo/foo`) wherever a package is named: `--package` on `add`, `matrix` and `release`, changeset entries, `pre.json` keys, group members, `[[package]]` and `[[package-set]]` `match`, `product-package` and `[[release.artifact]] package`. A bare name and the slash form are unaffected.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    },\ndocs/specs/workspace.json:23:      \"description\": \"Display and selector form: the bare manifest name, or `<ecosystem>/<name>` once another ecosystem declares the same name. JSON output, messages, changeset entries and `pre.json` keys use it; `<