-48a9-afd6-a7554fdb94e0","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:09:03.097Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-canonical-config","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"worktree-t06-canonical-config","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"9ba4eec0-b00e-48a9-afd6-a7554fdb94e0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f5cf9b4b-3262-4a4b-a98f-8654c9cfb941","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LhrRhd9Qe2UwNeFERfTaQP","type":"tool_result","content":"    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-ID-05\",\n      \"criterion\": \"A `[[fixed-group]]` or `[[linked-group]]` member written `cargo/foo` resolves to package `foo` when a Cargo manifest declares `foo`, promoted or not, through the same selector resolver used for `--package` and changesets; a member naming an ecosystem with no such manifest fails loading with E108, and a bare member name ambiguous across ecosystems fails loading with E103 (not E108). A group that names one package twice, under the same spelling or under two of its native names, fails loading with E250.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-CFG-01\",\n      \"criterion\": \"For each package, the first ecosystem-prefixed `[[package]]` rule whose ecosystem the package actually has a manifest in and whose name matches applies, regardless of declaration order relative to bare rules; a prefixed rule for an ecosystem the package has no manifest in never applies, even to a same-named package in another ecosystem. If no prefixed rule applies, the first matching bare rule applies.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-CFG-03\",\n      \"criterion\": \"A bare `[[package]]` rule that would apply to a promoted package fails loading with E103 listing the qualified candidates; prefixed rules for the same packages load normally.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-CFG-08\",\n      \"criterion\": \"A bare `[[package]]` rule matching packages whose manifests span two or more ecosystems, such as a dual-manifest package, emits one non-fatal `bare-rule-matches-multiple-ecosystems` warning; prefixed rules and `[[package-set]]` rules never emit it.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    },\n- `[[package]]` rules use `config::resolve::resolve_package_config`: two linear passes over the rules in declaration order, prefixed rules first, then bare. It never sorts the rules. A bare rule that reaches a promoted name is an `AmbiguousName` error, using `ResolvedConfig::promoted_siblings`.\n- `matches` is a weak \"could be the same package\" relation, not equality:\n  - Different names never match.\n  - A bare id matches any id with the same name, in either direction: bare is an ecosystem wildcard.\n  - Two prefixed ids match only when their ecosystems are equal.\n- A dual-manifest package can have different native names. `IdentityIndex` resolves each ecosystem/name to its owner; the weak `matches` relation alone does not establish distribution identity or ownership.\n\n## Resolving ambiguity\n\nA workspace can hold `cargo/foo` and `npm/foo` as separate packages; ambiguity is resolved where a lookup happens. Qualified selectors work before and after promotion, and the colon form is rejected with E316. Canonical-only new references are planned in [the v1 design](polyglot-v1.md), not implemented by today's parser.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"beaf2776-5dab-448b-826d-c822c49a7164","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:09:03.588Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-ID-05\",\n      \"criterion\": \"A `[[fixed-group]]` or `[[linked-group]]` member written `cargo/foo` resolves to package `foo` when a Cargo manifest declares `foo`, promoted or not, through the same selector resolver used for `--package` and changesets; a member naming an ecosystem with no such manifest fails loading with E108, and a bare member name ambiguous across ecosystems fails loading with E103 (not E108). A group that names one package twice, under the same spelling or under two of its native names, fails loading with E250.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-CFG-01\",\n      \"criterion\": \"For each package, the first ecosystem-prefixed `[[package]]` rule whose ecosystem the package actually has a manifest in and whose name matches applies, regardless of declaration order relative to bare rules; a prefixed rule for an ecosystem the package has no manifest in never applies, even to a same-named package in another ecosystem. If no prefixed rule applies, the first matching bare rule applies.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-CFG-03\",\n      \"criterion\": \"A bare `[[package]]` rule that would apply to a promoted package fails loading with E103 listing the qualified candidates; prefixed rules for the same packages load normally.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-CFG-08\",\n      \"criterion\": \"A bare `[[package]]` rule matching packages whose manifests span two or more ecosystems, such as a dual-manifest package, emits one non-fatal `bare-rule-matches-multiple-ecosystems` warning; prefixed rules and `[[package-set]]` rules never emit it.\",\n      \"is_error_case\": true\n    },\n- `[[package]]` rules use `config::resolve::resolve_package_config`: two linear passes over the rules in declaration order, prefixed rules first, then bare. It never sorts the rules. A bare rule that reaches a promoted name is an `AmbiguousName` error, using `ResolvedConfig::promoted_siblings`.\n- `matches` is a weak \"could be the same package\" relation, not equality:\n  - Different names never match.\n  - A bare id matches any id with the same name, in either direction: bare is an ecosystem wildcard.\n  - Two prefixed ids match only when their ecosystems are equal.\n- A dual-manifest package can have different native names. `IdentityIndex` resolves each ecosystem/name to its owner; the weak `matches` relation alone does not establish distribution identity or ownership.\n\n## Resolving ambiguity\n\nA workspace can hold `cargo/foo` and `npm/foo` as separate packages; ambiguity is resolved where a lookup happens. Qualified selectors work before and after promotion, and the colon form is rejected with E316. Canonical-only new references are planned in [the v1 design](polyglot-v1.md), not implemented by today's parser.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"4951155f-79ce-4147-a16c-86ef6b9f807f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-canonical-config","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-canonical-config","branch":"worktree-t06-canonical-config","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":27,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-canonical-config","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9ba4eec0-b00e-48a9-afd6-a7554fdb94e0","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-canonical-config","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"worktree-t06-canonical-config","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
