{"parentUuid":"e2da4e36-18d9-4bdf-96b3-506e894e4375","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFvBU9jnwxZnumyojC6M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #272 (E317) is open and ready for review, and #271 is green and ready to merge. #272's hosted CI is still running.\n\n**#272: a package in `callisto.toml` without its ecosystem is now E317**\n- **What changed:** a bare package name is rejected with the `eco/name` form shown. The same applies to `[[package]]` and `[[package-set]]` `match`, and to `product-package` and `[[release.artifact]] package`.\n- **Exceptions:** the native name of a platform package stays valid in a group. Changeset entries and `pre.json` keys keep native names.\n- **This repo:** its own `callisto.toml` is converted. The specs, `docs/config.md`, `docs/errors.md` (E317, 242 codes) and the identity note are updated.\n- **Tests:** fixtures use the qualified form, and new tests cover each rejected position and the CLI path. I removed the tests that could only write a bare rule, since a loaded config can no longer contain one. The two group tests about one package under two spellings now use a dual Cargo and npm package.\n- **Verified:** `just ci` passes locally (the log's `exit=0`, coverage 92.71%). The commit is signed and the PR is not a draft.\n- **Breaking:** it needs a minor bump on the CLI. A user's existing bare group members will fail until they add the prefix.\n- **Cleanup caught:** my scripted conversion altered two unrelated comments (`cargo/npm/twine` in `runner.rs` and one in the init tests). I restored them before committing.\n\n**Left for the next slice (T06 PR 4):** the PR body records this on purpose. With bare rules gone, three things are unreachable but still in the code:\n- The second bare pass in `resolve_package_config`.\n- `ResolvedConfig::promoted_siblings`.\n- The emission of the `bare-rule-matches-multiple-ecosystems` diagnostic.\n\nI held back because removing that diagnostic touches a code that appears in reports, so it goes with the rule-matching-through-the-identity-index change. That slice also removes the dead `from_groups`, `resolve_unique` and `resolve_human`.\n\nNext I'll watch #272's CI, then start T06 PR 4. Tell me if you'd rather I do the scheduled-`cargo deny`-style hygiene items first.\n\nresult: PR #272 (bare package names in `callisto.toml` rejected with E317) is open, signed and not a draft, with local CI green and hosted CI running, and #271 (MSRV, weekly advisories, dependabot) is green and ready for you to merge."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":797,"cache_read_input_tokens":263008,"output_tokens":858,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":797,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":858,"cache_read_input_tokens":263008,"cache_creation_input_tokens":797,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":797},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"204d827b-d4ce-4370-b117-0dacbc137218","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFvBTmv4aji2mXTSPt9v","requestRef":"fb0f2062-4824-417c-bf81-065d44cb2efe","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c70ddd4f-ef44-46bb-9c94-9196eb1edb8d","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:15:41.578Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-canonical-config","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","