Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/pre-mode-noop","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"worktree-pre-mode-noop","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"82f6cfd0-9bf1-4812-bfd0-61009676e5ab","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9a90d84d-4481-4fb3-9d31-62c096829dab","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0193Moudt1utUYMjYp377aHw","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/specs/release.json:145:      \"criterion\": \"`release plan --from-release-commit <sha> --decision <path>` takes the package and version roster from the decision file committed in that commit. It does not re-run changeset, group, cascade or pre-release selection.\"\ndocs/architecture/polyglot-v1.md:20:- A bare name in a changeset or `pre.json` resolves through established ownership; ambiguous input fails with an actionable diagnostic. Persisted release documents are already canonical-only.\ndocs/specs/cli.json:43:        \"`pre enter` while pre.json's mode is already `pre`.\",\ndocs/specs/cli.json:44:        \"`pre exit` after prerelease mode was already exited, or with no .changeset/pre.json.\"\ndocs/specs/cli.json:320:      \"criterion\": \"`callisto pre enter <tag>` writes .changeset/pre.json with mode `pre`, the tag and each package's initial version; `callisto pre exit` sets its mode to `exit`. When pre.json already exists with mode `exit`, `pre enter` resumes the cycle: it keeps the existing `initialVersions` and `cha\ndocs/specs/cli.json:324:      \"criterion\": \"`pre enter` while pre.json's mode is `pre` exits 1 naming the next step; `pre exit` after prerelease mode was already exited exits 1 naming the next step; `pre exit` with no .changeset/pre.json exits 1 naming `callisto pre enter <tag>`.\",\ndocs/architecture/versioning.md:12:- `VersionPlan` (`crates/callisto-graph/src/plan.rs`) is the whole change: bumps, dependency spec rewrites, platform manifest writes, owner `optionalDependencies` pins, changelog sections, consumed changesets, `pre.json` updates and diagnostics. It is in memory only (no `Serialize`).\ndocs/architecture/versioning.md:23:- Apply refreshes affected lockfiles and stages generated version state before consuming changesets or exiting `pre.json`. It stages input deletions with `git rm --cached --ignore-unmatch` before removing the files from disk, so a failed index update leaves the inputs available for recovery. A \ndocs/specs/versioning.json:131:      \"criterion\": \"All package members of a `[[fixed-group]]` receive the group's highest severity and one shared version, computed the same grammar- and pre-release-aware way as any other bump (VER-PRE-03): the alignment base is the on-disk version of the group's released member (a member with a \ndocs/specs/versioning.json:162:      \"criterion\": \"`pre enter` fails when the tag is empty or whitespace, or when `.changeset/pre.json` exists with mode `pre` (also under `--dry-run`); when it exists with mode `exit`, `pre enter` instead resumes the cycle under the new tag, keeping its recorded `initialVersions` and `changesets`\ndocs/specs/versioning.json:167:      \"criterion\": \"In pre mode, a bumped package's version is its `initialVersions` entry bumped by its severity plus `-{tag}.N`, where N starts at 0 and increments while the release part is unchanged (0.1.0 with a minor changeset and tag `beta` gives 0.2.0-beta.0, then 0.2.0-beta.1); PEP 440 pack\ndocs/specs/versioning.json:171:      \"criterion\": \"In pre mode, `version` never deletes a changeset from disk. A changeset whose id is not yet in `pre.json`'s `changesets` list counts toward severity, produces a changelog entry, and has its id added to `changesets`; a changeset whose id is already there still counts toward sever\ndocs/specs/versioning.json:188:      \"criterion\": \"A snapshot writes manifests and refreshes each active ecosystem's existing lockfile, unconditionally (there is no `--no-refresh-lockfiles` for `snapshot`), so a subsequent locked install resolves against the snapshot version; it ignores and keeps pending changesets, writes no ch\ndocs/specs/versioning.json:266:      \"criterion\": \"`version --emit-decision <path>` writes the release decision JSON to `<path>` relative to the workspace root after the plan has been applied successfully: `schemaVersion` 2, a digest, and one entry per canonical manifest of each bumped package (ecosystem-qualified name, target v\ndocs/specs/versioning.json:280:      \"criterion\": \"Outside `mode: pre`, after planning but before any write, `version` refuses with E121 when a canonical manifest's on-disk effective version differs from its version at `HEAD`, or when its effective version staged in the git index differs from `HEAD`, provided a changeset remains\ndocs/specs/versioning.json:294:      \"criterion\": \"When E121 checks a staged canonical manifest outside prerelease mode, `version` compares its effective version in the Git index as well as the working tree against `HEAD`. It refuses if either copy contains an uncommitted version change, even when the other copy matches `HEAD`; \ndocs/errors.md:180:| E114 | Failed to parse `.changeset/pre.json` | Check that .changeset/pre.json is valid JSON and was not partially written. Delete the file and re-run `callisto pre enter` to recover. |\ndocs/errors.md:181:| E115 | Failed to read `.changeset/pre.json` | Check that .changeset/pre.json is readable. Delete the file and re-run `callisto pre enter` to recover. |\ndocs/errors.md:186:| E121 | A canonical manifest's on-disk or staged version differs from its version at `HEAD` while release inputs remain in `HEAD` or the working tree, or a staged version change remains outside pre mode | Inspect `git diff` and `git diff --cached`. If these are correct outputs from an interrupted run, finish \ndocs/errors.md:240:| E207 | Computed bump for a package would move its version backwards | This indicates a corrupted alignment base (bad tag, pre.json, or group config); verify release state before retrying. |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8d5c0b5c-0396-4a78-af67-e75fd8e59afe","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:25:54.536Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"docs/specs/release.json