{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","hash":"8fa7fa635481c52725d414ba525ca329c4898eec750a8b0132748ee58bd5cf64","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Updating the spec, error docs, release-pr criterion, and adding the changeset."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013C2AjQ5VQUbLUT7ZkS15nu","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/15c732d1/tmp/docs_pre.py","content":"import re\n\n\ndef sub(path, old, new):\n    s = open(path).read()\n    if old not in s:\n        print('MISSING in', path, ':', old[:80])\n        return\n    open(path, 'w').write(s.replace(old, new, 1))\n\n\nv = 'docs/specs/versioning.json'\nsub(v,\n    \"a changeset whose id is already there still counts toward severity and the prerelease counter (VER-PRE-03) but produces no additional changelog entry. The `allow-empty-changesets`/`--strict` handling from VER-AGG-06 triggers only when no changeset -- new or already recorded -- resolves to a package this run, not merely when nothing new was added.\",\n    \"a changeset whose id is already there is not pending again: a package named only by recorded changesets is not bumped, so a rerun with nothing new changes nothing, and a package named by a new changeset still counts the recorded ones toward its severity. The `allow-empty-changesets`/`--strict` handling from VER-AGG-06 triggers when no changeset in pre mode is new.\")\n\nc = 'docs/specs/cli.json'\ns = open(c).read()\nm = re.search(r'\"criterion\": \"`release-pr decide` fails in these cases: ', s)\nprint('cli criterion found' if m else 'cli criterion NOT FOUND')\ns = s.replace('`release-pr decide` fails in these cases: ', '`release-pr decide` fails in these cases: pre mode (E318, because a release PR cannot consume changesets kept by pre mode), ', 1)\nopen(c, 'w').write(s)\n\ne = 'docs/errors.md'\ns = open(e).read()\nrow = [l for l in s.split('\\n') if l.startswith('| E317 |') or l.startswith('| E316 |')][-1]\nnew = '| E318 | `release-pr decide` was run while `.changeset/pre.json`\\'s mode is `pre` | Release prereleases locally with `callisto version` and `callisto release`, or run `callisto pre exit` before opening a release PR. |'\ns = s.replace(row, row + '\\n' + new, 1)\ns = re.sub(r'(\\d+) numeric E#### codes total', lambda mo: str(int(mo.group(1)) + 1) + ' numeric E#### codes total', s, count=1)\nopen(e, 'w').write(s)\nprint('done')\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QBQiuU9voAb3YY4PYPRX6y","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/pre-mode-noop/.changeset/pre-mode-no-repeat-bump.md","content":"---\ncallisto-cli: minor\n---\n\nIn pre-release mode, `version` no longer bumps a package again when its only changesets are already recorded in `pre.json`: a rerun with nothing new changes nothing, and `status` stops reporting it as pending. A new changeset produces the next prerelease. `release-pr decide` now refuses pre-release mode with E318 and a local-release fix, instead of opening a pull request that cannot release.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
