ly prepends a `## {version}` section under the `# {package}` heading of its changelog (default `CHANGELOG.md` in the package directory, overridable with `changelog`), creating the file if missing and keeping CRLF line endings; a changelog that already has that heading is left unchanged.\"","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2fec8b6a-5bf2-419e-b23b-f7da7d10954a","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:36:44.378Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"docs/errors.md:31:| E019 | Format-preserving write would not round-trip | Ensure CST document retains formatting structure. |\ndocs/specs/versioning.json:113:      \"criterion\": \"A spec that no longer covers the new version is rewritten to it, keeping the operator and precision for Cargo and npm (`^1.2` becomes `^2.0` for 2.0.0), or to the exact version for npm when `preserve-npm-ranges = false`. A runtime, optional, build or peer dependent that is itself released in this run, for any reason, has every such spec on a bumped internal dependenc\ndocs/specs/versioning.json:121:      \"criterion\": \"A Python dependency range on a package released with its dependent is rewritten to cover the new version: `==`, `~=` and `>=` keep their operator; a two-clause `>=X,<Y` range becomes `>=NEW` with an upper bound one minor above NEW when the original spanned a single minor (`>=0.1.0,<0.2`) and the next major otherwise; and a Poetry caret or tilde becomes the equivalent\ndocs/specs/versioning.json:192:      \"criterion\": \"For every workspace dependency whose current spec does not cover the snapshot version, `snapshot` rewrites that spec using the source declaration's manifest ecosystem and declared key or spelling, including Cargo aliases. Inherited Cargo declarations are rewritten in the root manifest of the Cargo workspace that governs the member rather than the member manifest. A s\ndocs/specs/versioning.json:204:      \"criterion\": \"Before writing a package or platform manifest, apply reads its current version: equal to the planned `from` it is written