{"parentUuid":"cbde7305-cab8-4c8d-a945-6bcdda40b1a5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFwo8JWGdYFKSUY24tby","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LPg3ai5hTaGeuHVfg3YY28","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/range-hard-stop/.changeset/stop-on-unrewritable-range.md","content":"---\ncallisto-cli: minor\n---\n\n`version` and `snapshot` now stop with E319 before writing anything when a dependency range that consumers install would keep excluding the new version cannot be rewritten, such as a Cargo `>=1.2.0, <2.0.0` range after a major bump. It used to warn, release the dependent anyway and leave an unresolvable range. An npm range with a prerelease clause, such as `^2.0.0-next.0` left over from a prerelease cycle, is now rewritten like any other (`^3.0.0`). Dev dependencies still only warn.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":513,"cache_read_input_tokens":408161,"output_tokens":1019,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":513,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1019,"cache_read_input_tokens":408161,"cache_creation_input_tokens":513,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":513},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01LPg3ai5hTaGeuHVfg3YY28":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/range-hard-stop/.changeset/stop-on-unrewritable-range.md","content":"---\ncallisto-cli: minor\n---\n\n`version` and `snapshot` now stop with E319 bef