"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/dist-tag-snapshot","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"worktree-dist-tag-snapshot","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"8e1255da-2829-4a47-a18c-92c09e08f826","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1ca2ef62-2f70-44a5-90cb-152dc6d95e66","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014eyrPePqdfzUr8fmnX1y6Y","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/architecture/polyglot-v1.md:47:Registry identity is separate from read/upload routes and native authentication configuration. Specify public PyPI first; decide authenticated private indexes and HTML-only indexes explicitly. Mutable npm dist-tags are channel labels, not distribution versions; channel verification/promotion policy is an owner decision, not implicit rollback.\ndocs/specs/release.json:205:      \"criterion\": \"npm publish picks its tool from the workspace that owns the package and runs there. The owner is the nearest directory at or above the package whose `package.json` declares `workspaces` or that has a `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, else for a package no workspace declares the nearest directory with a lockfile, else the root; a lockfile bes\ndocs/specs/cli.json:49:      \"signature\": \"callisto snapshot --tag <TAG> [--strict]\",\ndocs/specs/cli.json:52:        \"--tag missing (usage error, exit 2).\",\ndocs/specs/cli.json:329:      \"criterion\": \"`callisto snapshot --tag <tag>` sets each SemVer package's manifest version to `0.0.0-<tag>-<short HEAD sha>` and each PEP 440 package's to `0.0.0.dev0+<tag>.<short HEAD sha>`, prints each `from → to`, and leaves changesets in place.\"\ndocs/architecture/release.md:77:These reads are version-level checks, not proof of identical bytes or the npm dist-tag. Registry endpoints must be HTTPS. Read-only observations retry 429, 5xx, rate-limited 403, and transport failures with backoff and `Retry-After`. Effects are never blindly retried; outbound commands have deadlines.\ndocs/specs/versioning.json:24:      \"signature\": \"callisto snapshot --tag <TAG> [--strict] [--dry-run]\",\ndocs/specs/versioning.json:184:      \"criterion\": \"`callisto snapshot --tag <tag>` sets every workspace package, and every attached platform package and fixed-group platform manifest, to a snapshot version built from the same tag and sha7 (the first 7 characters of HEAD) in the package's own grammar: `0.0.0-{tag}-{sha7}` for a SemVer package, `0.0.0.dev0+{tag}.{sha7}` for a Pep\ndocs/releasing.md:118:Registry checks confirm version presence, not identical bytes or the npm dist-tag. A Python release is complete only when every built wheel and sdist is on the index; a partly uploaded one is finished by uploading the missing files, and a sealed build also compares each file's digest. See [publishing limits](publishing.md#current-python-support-limits).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6ea43762-c4b2-46a4-ad79-933d012cb519","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:42:47.036Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"docs/architecture/polyglot-v1.md:47:Registry identity is separate from read/upload routes and native authentication configuration. Specify public PyPI first; decide authenticated private indexes and HTML-only indexes explicitly. Mutable npm dist-tags are channel labels, not distribution versions; channel verification/promotion policy is an owner decision, not implicit rollback.\ndocs/specs/release.json:205:      \"criterion\": \"npm publish picks its tool from the workspace that owns the package and runs there. The owner is the nearest directory at or above the package whose `package.json` declares `workspaces` or that has a `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, else for a package no workspace declares the nearest directory with a lockfile, else the root; a lockfile bes\ndocs/specs/cli.json:49:      \"signature\": \"callisto snapshot --tag <TAG> [--strict]\",\ndocs/specs/cli.json:52:        \"--tag missing (usage error, exit 2).\",\ndocs/specs/cli.json:329:      \"criterion\": \"`callisto snapshot --tag <tag>` sets each SemVer package's manifest version to `0.0.0-<tag>-<short HEAD sha>` and each PEP 440 package's to `0.0.0.dev0+<tag>.<short HEAD sha>`, prints each `from → to`, and leaves changesets in place.\"\ndocs/architecture/release.md:77:These reads are version-level checks, not proof of identical bytes or the npm dist-tag. Registry endpoints must be HTTPS. Read-only observations retry 429, 5xx, rate-limited 403, and transport failures with backoff and `Retry-After`. Effects are never blindly retried; outbound commands have deadlines.\ndocs/specs/versioning.json:24:      \"signature\": \"callisto snapshot --tag <TAG> [--strict] [--dry-run]\",\ndocs/specs/versioning.json:184:      \"criterion\": \"`callisto snapshot --tag <tag>` sets every workspace package, and every attached platform package and fixed-group platform manifest, to a snapshot version built from the same tag and sha7 (the first 7 characters of HEAD) in the package's own grammar: `0.0.0-{tag}-{sha7}` for a SemVer package, `0.0.0.dev0+{tag}.{sha7}` for a Pep\ndocs/releasing.md:118:Registry checks confirm version presence, not identical bytes or the npm dist-tag. A Python release is complete only when every built wheel and sdist is on the index; a partly uploaded one is finished by uploading the missing files, and a sealed build also compares each file's digest. See [publishing limits](publishing.md#current-python-support-limits).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"34fb08b4-01f7-4291-bfaa-2e570b4e8760","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/dist-tag-snapshot","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/dist-tag-snapshot","branch":"worktree-dist-tag-snapshot","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":4,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"