pN3","requestRef":"645284a5-7191-47bb-ba94-bb34af4acb77","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c7a832d9-2ae0-4547-9ccf-613a19ed7f6a","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:49:44.201Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-dead-bare","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"worktree-t06-dead-bare","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"c7a832d9-2ae0-4547-9ccf-613a19ed7f6a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"48abfd8d-ba79-4e5c-a41d-2b5b7415c485","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TVRTjNANgpfZzUdz92hMYc","type":"tool_result","content":"- `[[package]]` rules use `config::resolve::resolve_package_config`: the first rule in declaration order whose ecosystem the package has and whose name matches. It never sorts the rules. Config rejects a rule without its ecosystem (E317), so the bare-rule second pass is unreachable from a loaded config.\n1. `config::load` reads `callisto.toml` (absent means empty) and calls `config::resolve`, which does all validation and defaulting. Callers holding a `RawConfig` in memory call `resolve` directly.\n2. `ManifestWalkResolver::build` discovers projects, assigns ids (`IdentityIndex`), attaches platform packages and applies per-package config.\n3. `GroupTable::resolve` binds group members to ids, then names promoted into several ecosystems are recorded as `promoted_siblings`.\n4. The tag index is built lazily, on the first `Workspace::tags` call.\n\n        \"Baseline: IdentityIndex.resolve_id resolves native names; the status helpers no longer use PackageId::resolve_unique, which is unused outside its tests. GroupTable::from_groups is deprecated and has no caller. Rules and packages match only the primary name, so a dual-manifest owner's npm name never matches a [[package]] rule.\",\n        \"Match [[package]] and [[package-set]] rules through the identity index so a dual-manifest owner's secondary native name applies. Share group membership validation between GroupTable::resolve and try_from_groups, and delete the dead from_groups, resolve_unique and resolve_human with a Breaking note.\",\n\n/// Prefixed rule (npm:pkg, OFF policy) must win over Bare rule (pkg, conservative)\n/// even when the Bare rule is declared first in callisto.toml.\n/// With single-pass lookup: the Bare rule (declared first) wins -> conservative applied.\n/// With resolve_package_config (two-pass): the Prefixed rule wins -> OFF applied.\n///\n/// Two AtomicBool flags:\n/// - invoked: true if infer() was called at all (proves the package is pre-1.0 and\n///   pre-major-inference was consulted; distinguishes OFF-applied from never-called).\n    // Two-pass resolve_package_config: pass 1 finds npm:pkg (Prefixed) -> OFF applied.\n    // The package's own manifest is npm (`make_pkg`'s ecosystem-derived-from-id, via a\n    // Prefixed id here) so the `npm:pkg` rule is actually ecosystem-eligible, not just\n    // name-eligible -- this test is about two-pass declaration-order precedence, not\n    // about a rule applying to a package that was never really in that ecosystem.\n    std::fs::write(\n            root.join(\"callisto.toml\"),","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"fba687bc-2890-4bad-b622-d8fd7cfd35b6","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:49:44.606Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"- `[[package]]` rules use `config::resolve::resolve_package_config`: the first rule in declaration order whose ecosystem the package has and whose name matches. It never sorts the rules. Config rejects a rule without its ecosystem (E317), so the bare-rule second pass is unreachable from a loaded config.\n1. `config::load` reads `callisto.toml` (absent means empty) and calls `config::resolve`, which does all validation and defaulting. Callers holding a `RawConfig` in memory call `resolve` directly.\n2. `ManifestWalkResolver::build` discovers projects, assigns ids (`IdentityIndex`), attaches platform packages and applies per-package config.\n3. `GroupTable::resolve` binds group members to ids, then names promoted into several ecosystems are recorded as `promoted_siblings`.\n4. The tag index is built lazily, on the first `Workspace::tags` call.\n\n        \"Baseline: IdentityIndex.resolve_id resolves native names; the status helpers no longer use PackageId::resolve_unique, which is unused outside its tests. GroupTable::from_groups is deprecated and has no caller. Rules and packages match only the primary name, so a dual-manifest owner's npm name never matches a [[package]] rule.\",\n        \"Match [[package]] and [[package-set]] rules through the identity index so a dual-manifest owner's secondary native name applies. Share group membership validation between GroupTable::resolve and try_from_groups, and delete the dead from_groups, resolve_unique and resolve_human with a Breaking note.\",\n\n/// Prefixed rule (npm:pkg, OFF policy) must win over Bare rule (pkg, conservative)\n/// even when the Bare rule is declared first in callisto.toml.\n/// With single-pass lookup: the Bare rule (declared first) wins -> conservative applied.\n/// With resolve_package_config (two-pass): the Prefixed rule wins -> OFF applied.\n///\n/// Two AtomicBool flags:\n/// - invoked: true if infer() was called at all (proves the package is pre-1.0 and\n///   pre-major-inference was consulted; distinguishes OFF-applied from never-called).\n    // Two-pass resolve_package_config: pass 1 finds npm:pkg (Prefixed) -> OFF applied.\n    // The package's own manifest is npm (`make_pkg`'s ecosystem-derived-from-id, via a\n    // Prefixed id here) so the `npm:pkg` rule is actually ecosystem-eligible, not just\n    // name-eligible -- this test is about two-pass declaration-order precedence, not\n    // about a rule applying to a package that was never really in that ecosystem.\n    std::fs::write(\n            root.join(\"callisto.toml\"),","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"2c1ee130-27d4-4873-85c3-5cc51cb019e2","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-dead-bare","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-dead-bare","branch":"worktree-t06-dead-bare","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":10,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-dead-bare","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c7a832d9-2ae0-4547-9ccf-613a19ed7f6a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-dead-bare","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"worktree-t06-dead-bare","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
