{"parentUuid":"480e8e6f-7140-4ecc-9c85-950389bfcacc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFxoETTyiD2PtcyZhAct","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JjPDpfZcpKr2LfkrmTfaqU","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\ndef rep(path, old, new):\n    s=open(path).read()\n    assert old in s,(path,old[:60])\n    open(path,'w').write(s.replace(old,new,1))\nrep('docs/architecture/identity.md',' Config rejects a rule without its ecosystem (E317), so the bare-rule second pass is unreachable from a loaded config.',' Config rejects a rule without its ecosystem (E317), so every rule is ecosystem-qualified.')\nrep('docs/architecture/identity.md','3. `GroupTable::resolve` binds group members to ids, then names promoted into several ecosystems are recorded as `promoted_siblings`.\\n4. The tag index','3. `GroupTable::resolve` binds group members to ids.\\n4. The tag index')\nrep('docs/projects/V1-SYSTEM-HARDENING.json',\"Baseline: IdentityIndex.resolve_id resolves native names; the status helpers no longer use PackageId::resolve_unique, which is unused outside its tests. GroupTable::from_groups is deprecated and has no caller. Rules and packages match only the primary name\",\"Baseline: IdentityIndex.resolve_id resolves native names. Rules and packages match only the primary name\")\nrep('docs/projects/V1-SYSTEM-HARDENING.json',\" Share group membership validation between GroupTable::resolve and try_from_groups, and delete the dead from_groups, resolve_unique and resolve_human with a Breaking note.\",\" Share group membership validation between GroupTable::resolve and try_from_groups.\")\nrep('crates/callisto-graph/src/walk/tests.rs',\"a distinct-id count of 2 is required for ResolvedConfig.promoted_siblings' derivation to retain this name\",\"a distinct-id count of 2 is required to retain this name\")\nPYEOF\npython3 -c \"import json;json.load(open('docs/projects/V1-SYSTEM-HARDENING.json'))\" && echo ok; /usr/bin/git rm -q crates/callisto-graph/tests/cross_ecosystem_diagnostic_test.rs 2>&1 | tail -1; rg -n 'cross_ecosystem_diagnostic' . --glob '!target' | head","description":"Update docs and plan, remove vacuous diagnostic test file"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1190,"cache_read_input_tokens":475224,"output_tokens":1047,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1190,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1047,"cache_read_input_tokens":475224,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1190,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1190},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01JjPDpfZcpKr2LfkrmTfaqU":{"command":"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\ndef rep(path, old, new):\n    s=open(path).read()\n    assert old in s,(path,old[:60])\n    open(path,'w').write(s.replace(old,new,1))\nrep('docs/architecture/identity.md',' Config rejects a rule without its ecosystem (E317), so the bare-rule second pass is unreachable from a loaded config.',' Config rejects a rule without its ecosystem (E317), so every rule is ecosystem-qualified.')\nrep('docs/architecture/identity.md','3. `GroupTable::resolve` binds group members to ids, then names promoted into several ecosystems are recorded as `promoted_siblings`.\\n4. The tag index','3. `GroupTable::resolve` binds group members to ids.\\n4. The tag index')\nrep('docs/projects/V1-SYSTEM-HARDENING.json',\"Baseline: IdentityIndex.resolve_id resolves native names; the status helpers no longer use PackageId::resolve_unique, which is unused outside its tests. Gr