{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01RnkWesCzJyeY97T2UxQPcQ","lastSequenceNum":4761,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"b93a07bc-230a-46df-a8a2-d6de2025f2b8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFykgtyctL7gueGmi5H5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01C5Wq2VFmUdkKok5ccWhqRw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"/usr/bin/git push -u origin worktree-py-dev-warn:feat/status-inferred-release-and-failed-command-tail 2>&1 | tail -1; gh pr create --base main --head feat/status-inferred-release-and-failed-command-tail --title \"feat(status): warn about inferred releases with no changeset and show the failed command on indeterminate errors\" --body \"Two accepted decisions from the v1 review.\n\nInferred-only releases: the managed release pull request reads changesets only, so a \\`release-trigger = \\\"auto\\\"\\` package whose pending release comes from commits would never be released there. \\`status\\` now reports an \\`inferred-release-without-changeset\\` warning for it (new diagnostic code). A package a changeset names, or one bumped by a dependency or group, is not reported. It is a warning, so \\`status --check --strict\\` fails on it and plain \\`--check\\` does not.\n\nIndeterminate errors: E176 (provider observation indeterminate) and E157 (publish not yet visible) named no tool output. After a text-mode error, the CLI now prints the most recent failed command and the end of its stderr, 20 lines or 2 KiB, credentials redacted. It is print-only: no JSON field, receipt or persisted shape changes. The summary is the most recent non-zero command, so it can be an earlier probe; it is labelled that way. I did not reproduce an E176 with a real registry; the formatting and redaction are unit-tested and the wiring is one match in \\`main\\`.\n\nDropped: a Python dev-table warning. Those groups are already documented as not followed, and a warning for every dev-group dependency on a workspace member would fire on ordinary uv setups.\n\nTests: status warning with and without a changeset, tail line and byte caps, and token redaction. The CLI spec and \\`docs/errors.md\\` are updated.\n\nVerified: \\`just ci\\` passes locally.\" 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Push and open the W4 PR"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":954,"cache_read_input_tokens":526126,"output_tokens":783,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":954,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":783,"cache_read_input_tokens":526126,"cache_creation_input_tokens":954,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":954},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01C5Wq2VFmUdkKok5ccWhqRw":{"command":"/usr/bin/git push -u origin worktree-py-dev-warn:feat/status-inferred-release-and-failed-command-tail 2>&1 | tail -1; gh pr create --base main --head feat/status-inferred-release-and-failed-command-tail --title \"feat(status): warn about inferred releases with no changeset and show the failed command on indeterminate errors\" --body \"Two accepted decisions from the v1 review.\n\nInferred-only releases: the managed release pull request reads changesets only, so a \\`release-trigger = \\\"auto\\\"\\` package whose pending release comes from commits would never be released there. \\`status\\` now reports an \\`inferred-release-without-changeset\\` warning for it (new diagnostic code). A package a changeset names, or one bumped by a dependency or group, is not reported. It is a warning, so \\`status --check --strict\\` fails on it and plain \\`--check\\` does not.\n\nIndeterminate errors: E176 (provider observation indeterminate) and E157 (publish not yet visible) named no tool output. After a text-mode error, the CLI now prints the most recent failed command and the end of its stderr, 20 lines or 2 KiB, credentials redacted. It is print-only: no JSON field, receipt or persisted shape changes. The summary is the most recent non-zero command, so it can be an earlier probe; it is labelled that way. I did not reproduce an E176 with a real registry; the formatting and redaction are unit-tested and the wiring is one match in \\`main\\`.\n\nDropped: a Python dev-table warning. Those groups are already documented as not followed, and a warning for every dev-group dependency on a workspace member would fire on ordinary uv setups.\n\nTests: status warning with and without a changeset, tail line and byte caps, and token redaction. The CLI spec and \\`docs/errors.md\\` are updated.\n\nVerified: \\`just ci\\` passes locally.\" 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Push and open the W4 PR"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"177e9f61-8c44-4bb3-bcb9-319a5b2aa747","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFykgRCUnv1S1X86LkdM","requestRef":"0f54ed05-89b4-480f-80f9-6225540ff668","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c9bc0f8a-398c-40cb-9a41-aafc0b3cd53f","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:02:31.476Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/py-dev-warn","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"worktree-py-dev-warn","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
