/.claude/worktrees/t06-canonical-emission","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"worktree-t06-canonical-emission","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"d113ef61-d5b4-4d8f-bf33-ed9b4c864278","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f73ac011-449f-49f1-86f1-9e3c96614956","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RtjqXrtyhxzihT2h1G5r5i","type":"tool_result","content":"| A1 allow-list, dynamic only | One package, Cargo is the authority. Python version is derived with the same parser as maturin and verified. Accept stable and `-alpha.N`, `-beta.N`, `-rc.N`. Refuse every other prerelease form, build metadata and snapshots for a co-located PyPI output, before any write. A static `project.version` next to Cargo is refused (maturin does not catch drift) | Large. Mode\n| A2 allow-list, static allowed | Same, but a static `project.version` equal to the derived value is also accepted and Callisto rewrites both | Larger. Two writers, the grammar-per-write problem in `apply.rs`, and `uv.lock` refresh | Two sources of truth that can drift |\n| A3 keep E007 | Stay out of scope for v1. Fix the nondeterministic grammar order and make the help text say \"use separate directories\". No lockstep Cargo+PyPI | Small | The headline Rust-to-Python path stays manual, with silent crate/wheel skew possible |\n| A4 two packages in one directory | `Package::key` is the directory and the walker, tags, changelog and promotion assume one package per directory | Very large | Identity model change; E100/E101 interactions |\n\nLean: A1 if Maturin is in the v1 promise, otherwise A3 plus the small E007 fix. A2 and A4 add cost without a matching benefit. Owner questions: (1) is the allow-list acceptable, or must custom pre tags work for co-located packages; (2) refuse or ignore a static Python version that disagrees with Cargo; (3) refuse snapshots and `+build` for co-located PyPI outputs, or skip the PyPI output for them.\n\n## D01-B: canonical references and the legacy boundary\n\nState today (reproduced and source):\n\n| Surface | Accepts | Emits |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Release wire (decision, intent, snapshot, manifest, receipt) | `ecosystem/native-name` only | same |\n| `release --package` | qualified only; bare gives E227; colon accepted as an alias | n/a |\n| `product-package`, `[[release.artifact]] package` | qualified only; bare gives E197 | n/a |\n| Changesets, `callisto add`, config groups and rules, `pre.json`, `matrix --package` | bare, `eco:name`, `eco/name` (prefix case-insensitive) | bare when unpromoted, slash when promoted |\n| `status`, `version`, `matrix` output | n/a | bare when unpromoted, slash when promoted |\n| `callisto init` | n/a | always slash |\n\nColon is emitted nowhere. The real trap is promotion: a changeset `foo: minor` works until an unrelated `npm/foo` appears, then `status` reports an ambiguous-package error (reproduced; WS-ID-06). It fails loudly, not silently.\n\nFindings that change the scope:\n- A changeset entry names an owner package, not a distribution. In a dual Cargo+npm directory `x-core`, `cargo/x-core`, `npm/@x/core` and `@x/core` all write `x-core: minor`, and an entry naming both merges into one bump (reproduced). \"The canonical reference\" for an entry has no single answer.\n- Python selectors use the declared name (`pypi/Foo_Bar`); `foo-bar` and `pypi/foo-bar` give E102. PEP 503 normalization applies only to dependency-name lookup. Canonical-only must choose declared or normalized.\n- ADR 1 promises one-commit adoption and rollback with `@changesets/cli`. Canonical `npm/@scope/x` in `.changeset/*.md` and `pre.json` breaks that for npm users. `pre.json` is also changesets-compatible.\n- This repo dogfoods the bare forms: `callisto.toml` groups, all 8 `.changeset/*.md`, `AGENTS.md`/`CONTRIBUTING.md` (`--package callisto-cli:<bump>`), and 111 bare tags.\n- Blast radius if readers become strict: 166 colon literals in about 25 test files (mechanical), 192 bare `PackageId::parse` calls (mostly unit tests), roughly 26 bare `--package` args in CLI tests, and 24 of 236 spec criteria. T06 lists only 11 of them; WS-ID-07, WS-CFG-03/04/08, VER-PRE-01 and WS-ID-10 are missing.\n- There is no `migrate` or `doctor` command and no config schema version (`RawConfig` is `deny_unknown_fields`). Only Nx (`nx migrate`) and Lerna (`lerna repair`) ship one among the tools checked (web, from search summaries; not verified on the primary pages).\n\nOptions for the legacy-read boundary:\n\n| | Readers | Writers | Cost | Cost to users |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| M1 hard break | canonical only | canonical | Large: strict readers, 400+ fixtures, ~24 criteria | Every existing repo, this one included, fails on upgrade and users hand-edit. Breaks ADR 1 rollback |\n| M2 warn, then canonical on write | legacy accepted with a warning | canonical | Medium: warning plumbing, a diagnostic code, format-preserving rewrites | Smooth; two spellings persist until a deadline |\n| M3 explicit `callisto migrate` | strict after migration; old repos error with a pointer | canonical | Largest: new command, spec, tests, plus strict readers | Auditable one-command rewrite; adoption cost |\n| M4 only change writers | unchanged | canonical | Smallest | None; leaves the promotion trap and contradicts \"reject new bare aliases\" |\n| M5 split by surface | canonical required in config, groups, rules, reports, matrix keys, CLI args; changesets and `pre.json` keep native names and resolve at read time | canonical where unambiguous | Medium | Keeps ADR 1 interop; the promotion trap remains only in changesets, where it is loud |\n\nLean: M5, with colon rejected everywhere (never emitted, so nothing breaks) and an error that names the slash form. It keeps the owner's intent where identity matters (config, reports, CLI), respects ADR 1, and avoids a new command. If you want the owner text taken literally for every authored file, M3 is the only option with an auditable boundary and it should be scheduled as its own PR. Owner qu\n\n## D01-C: default tag template\n\nToday: `TagTemplate::default_for` renders `{display id}@{version}`, so `foo@1.0.0` while unpromoted and `cargo/foo@1.1.0` after a same-named sibling appears. The doc comment above it (`tag.rs:70`) says the opposite and is stale. Tags are one per published package, fixed groups do not share a tag, and a dual Cargo+npm package gets one tag named from the primary manifest (source: `derive.rs` `add_ta\n\nPrior art (web, primary docs, partly search summaries): every tool checked names tags `<native name><sep><version>` per package, with `v<version>` for a single or fixed unit. None qualifies a tag by ecosystem. Go is the only one that derives the tag from the directory (`subdir/vX.Y.Z`). No tool reads old-pattern tags automatically after a change; Callisto's `previous-tag-templates` plus ownership \n\n| | Existing repos | Promoted package | Second inference authority | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| T1 keep `{display id}@` (status quo) | History resolves | Namespace flips on promotion | Yes, the sibling scan | ADR 11 accepted this |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8591de8a-babc-4f42-bd25-cdbd6d3ac342","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:16:48.053Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"| A1 allow-list, dynamic only | One package, Cargo is the authority. Python version is derived with the same parser as maturin and verified. Accept stable and `-alpha.N`, `-beta.N`, `-rc.N`. Refuse every other prerelease form, build metadata and snapshots for a co-located PyPI output, before any write. A static `project.version` next to Cargo is refused (maturin does not catch drift) | Large. Mode\n| A2 allow-list, static allowed | Same, but a static `project.version` equal to the derived value is also accepted and Callisto rewrites both | Larger. Two writers, the grammar-per-write problem in `apply.rs`, and `uv.lock` refresh | Two sources of truth that can drift |\n| A3 keep E007 | Stay out of scope for v1. Fix the nondeterministic grammar order and make the help text say \"use separate directories\". No lockstep Cargo+PyPI | Small | The headline Rust-to-Python path stays manual, with silent crate/wheel skew possible |\n| A4 two packages in one directory | `Package::key` is the directory and the walker, tags, changelog and promotion assume one package per directory | Very large | Identity model change; E100/E101 interactions |\n\nLean: A1 if Maturin is in the v1 promise, otherwise A3 plus the small E007 fix. A2 and A4 add cost without a matching benefit. Owner questions: (1) is the allow-list acceptable, or must custom pre tags work for co-located packages; (2) refuse or ignore a static Python version that disagrees with Cargo; (3) refuse snapshots and `+build` for co-located PyPI outputs, or skip the PyPI output for them.\n\n## D01-B: canonical references and the legacy boundary\n\nState today (reproduced and source):\n\n| Surface | Accepts | Emits |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Release wire (decision, intent, snapshot, manifest, receipt) | `ecosystem/native-name` only | same |\n| `release --package` | qualified only; bare gives E227; colon accepted as an alias | n/a |\n| `product-package`, `[[release.artifact]] package` | qualified only; bare gives E197 | n/a |\n| Changesets, `callisto add`, config groups and rules, `pre.json`, `matrix --package` | bare, `eco:name`, `eco/name` (prefix case-insensitive) | bare when unpromoted, slash when promoted |\n| `status`, `version`, `matrix` output | n/a | bare when unpromoted, slash when promoted |\n| `callisto init` | n/a | always slash |\n\nColon is emitted nowhere. The real trap is promotion: a changeset `foo: minor` works until an unrelated `npm/foo` appears, then `status` reports an ambiguous-package error (reproduced; WS-ID-06). It fails loudly, not silently.\n\nFindings that change the scope:\n- A changeset entry names an owner package, not a distribution. In a dual Cargo+npm directory `x-core`, `cargo/x-core`, `npm/@x/core` and `@x/core` all write `x-core: minor`, and an entry naming both merges into one bump (reproduced). \"The canonical reference\" for an entry has no single answer.\n- Python selectors use the declared name (`pypi/Foo_Bar`); `foo-bar` and `pypi/foo-bar` give E102. PEP 503 normalization applies only to dependency-name lookup. Canonical-only must choose declared or normalized.\n- ADR 1 promises one-commit adoption and rollback with `@changesets/cli`. Canonical `npm/@scope/x` in `.changeset/*.md` and `pre.json` breaks that for npm users. `pre.json` is also changesets-compatible.\n- This repo dogfoods the bare forms: `callisto.toml` groups, all 8 `.changeset/*.md`, `AGENTS.md`/`CONTRIBUTING.md` (`--package callisto-cli:<bump>`), and 111 bare tags.\n- Blast radius if readers become strict: 166 colon literals in about 25 test files (mechanical), 192 bare `PackageId::parse` calls (mostly unit tests), roughly 26 bare `--package` args in CLI tests, and 24 of 236 spec criteria. T06 lists only 11 of them; WS-ID-07, WS-CFG-03/04/08, VER-PRE-01 and WS-ID-10 are missing.\n- There is no `migrate` or `doctor` command and no config schema version (`RawConfig` is `deny_unknown_fields`). Only Nx (`nx migrate`) and Lerna (`lerna repair`) ship one among the tools checked (web, from search summaries; not verified on the primary pages).\n\nOptions for the legacy-read boundary:\n\n| | Readers | Writers | Cost | Cost to users |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| M1 hard break | canonical only | canonical | Large: strict readers, 400+ fixtures, ~24 criteria | Every existing repo, this one included, fails on upgrade and users hand-edit. Breaks ADR 1 rollback |\n| M2 warn, then canonical on write | legacy accepted with a warning | canonical | Medium: warning plumbing, a diagnostic code, format-preserving rewrites | Smooth; two spellings persist until a deadline |\n| M3 explicit `callisto migrate` | strict after migration; old repos error with a pointer | canonical | Largest: new command, spec, tests, plus strict readers | Auditable one-command rewrite; adoption cost |\n| M4 only change writers | unchanged | canonical | Smallest | None; leaves the promotion trap and contradicts \"reject new bare aliases\" |\n| M5 split by surface | canonical required in config, groups, rules, reports, matrix keys, CLI args; changesets and `pre.json` keep native names and resolve at read time | canonical where unambiguous | Medium | Keeps ADR 1 interop; the promotion trap remains only in changesets, where it is loud |\n\nLean: M5, with colon rejected everywhere (never emitted, so nothing breaks) and an error that names the slash form. It keeps the owner's intent where identity matters (config, reports, CLI), respects ADR 1, and avoids a new command. If you want the owner text taken literally for every authored file, M3 is the only option with an auditable boundary and it should be scheduled as its own PR. Owner qu\n\n## D01-C: default tag template\n\nToday: `TagTemplate::default_for` renders `{display id}@{version}`, so `foo@1.0.0` while unpromoted and `cargo/foo@1.1.0` after a same-named sibling appears. The doc comment above it (`tag.rs:70`) says the opposite and is stale. Tags are one per published package, fixed groups do not share a tag, and a dual Cargo+npm package gets one tag named from the primary manifest (source: `derive.rs` `add_ta\n\nPrior art (web, primary docs, partly search summaries): every tool checked names tags `<native name><sep><version>` per package, with `v<version>` for a single or fixed unit. None qualifies a tag by ecosystem. Go is the only one that derives the tag from the directory (`subdir/vX.Y.Z`). No tool reads old-pattern tags automatically after a change; Callisto's `previous-tag-templates` plus ownership \n\n| | Existing repos | Promoted package | Second inference authority | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| T1 keep `{display id}@` (status quo) | History resolves | Namespace flips on promotion | Yes, the sibling scan | ADR 11 accepted this |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"4e97644b-4777-4cbb-ad17-85261b6c003