{"parentUuid":"2c981b2d-deeb-48c5-8454-89183e479ecf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgG2bauu1oDwRMmpEupWV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JVcQZmEMZhvuyNtExiWoX7","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"/usr/bin/git push -u origin worktree-edition-2024:chore/edition-2024 2>&1 | tail -1; gh pr create --base main --head chore/edition-2024 --title \"chore: move the workspace to edition 2024 and resolver 3\" --body \"Accepted hygiene item for 1.0. The workspace moves from edition 2021 to 2024 and from resolver 2 to 3. The MSRV (1.96) already supports both.\n\n\\`cargo fix --edition\\` applied its migration lints. Clippy's collapsible-if findings, which edition 2024's let-chains enable, are taken (7 in the model crate and more elsewhere; 35 files, roughly net zero lines).\n\nOne thing worth reviewing: edition 2024 makes \\`std::env::set_var\\` and \\`remove_var\\` unsafe, and the migration inserted \\`unsafe\\` blocks into two tests. The workspace forbids unsafe code, so those tests (secret redaction in cargo output and in a failed command's error text) now use \\`temp-env\\`, a small dev-dependency that sets and restores the variable under a lock. No production code changes.\n\nrustfmt is pinned to the 2021 style edition so formatting does not churn 332 hunks; it can be dropped separately.\n\nThe standalone \\`fuzz\\` crate stays on 2021 since it builds on nightly with cargo-fuzz and I could not verify it here.\n\nVerified: \\`just ci\\` passes locally.\" 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Push and open the edition PR"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":942,"cache_read_input_tokens":679244,"output_tokens":570,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":942,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":570,"cache_read_input_tokens":679244,"cache_creation_input_tokens":942,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":942},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01JVcQZmEMZhvuyNtExiWoX7":{"command":"/usr/bin/git push -u origin worktree-edition-2024:chore/edition-2024 2>&1 | tail -1; gh pr create --base main --head chore/edition-2024 --title \"chore: move the workspace to edition 2024 and resolver 3\" --body \"Accepted hygiene item for 1.0. The workspace moves from edition 2021 to 2024 and from resolver 2 to 3. The MSRV (1.96) already supports both.\n\n\\`cargo fix --edition\\` applied its migration lints. Clippy's collapsible-if findings, which edition 2024's let-chains enable, are taken (7 in the model crate and more elsewhere; 35 files, roughly net zero lines).\n\nOne thing worth reviewing: edition 2024 makes \\`std::env::set_var\\` and \\`remove_var\\` unsafe, and the migration inserted \\`unsafe\\` blocks into two tests. The workspace forbids unsafe code, so those tests (secret redaction in cargo output and in a failed command's error text) now use \\`temp-env\\`, a small dev-dependency that sets and restores the variable under a lock. No production code changes.\n\nrustfmt is pinned to the 2021 style edition so formatting does not churn 332 hunks; it can be dropped separately.\n\nThe standalone \\`fuzz\\` crate stays on 2021 since it builds on nightly with cargo-fuzz and I could not verify it here.\n\nVerified: \\`just ci\\` passes locally.\" 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Push and open the edition PR"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"f27b0462-7d4a-40b3-8a72-c561434adc9a","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgG2baPtsSBQhUyyETp8B","requestRef":"29f2a6f9-31d3-48c6-8faa-5dc75aec0ca